'''''Cyclophora azorensis''''' is a [[moth]] in the  family [[Geometridae]]. It is found on the [[Azores]].<ref>[https://web.archive.org/web/20151208010428/http://www.faunaeur.org/full_results.php?id=443978 Fauna Europaea]</ref>

The [[wingspan]] is 22–25&nbsp;mm. It is similar to ''[[Cyclophora maderensis]]'', but has broader wings and has a denser reddish irroration.

The larvae feed on ''[[Erica (plant)|Erica]]'' species.<ref>[http://www.lepiforum.de/lepiwiki.pl?Cyclophora_azorensis lepiforum.de]</ref>

