'''''Ramayana: Part 1'''''{{Efn|Released as '''''Namit Malhotra's Ramayana''''' with the tagline "Our Truth. Our History"<ref>{{Cite news |title=RAMAYANA UNVEILED |url=https://www.dneg.com/news/ramayana-unveiled |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250703213031/https://www.dneg.com/news/ramayana-unveiled |archive-date=3 July 2025 |access-date=3 July 2025 |publisher=[[DNEG]]}}</ref> in India and as '''''Ramayana: Rise of a Legend''''' worldwide.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.ign.com/movies/ramayana-rise-of-a-legend|title=Ramayana: Rise of a Legend|access-date=3 October 2026|website=[[IGN]]|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261016081145/https://www.ign.com/movies/ramayana-rise-of-a-legend|archive-date=16 October 2026|url-status=live}}</ref>}} is a 2026 Indian [[Hindi]]-language [[Epic film|epic]] [[fantasy film|mythological film]]<ref>{{cite web |first=Yola |last=Roberts |access-date=18 May 2024 |title=Namit Malhotra Film Industry Titan Brings Hindu Mythology To Hollywood |url=https://www.forbes.com/sites/yolarobert1/2024/05/18/film-industry-titan-brings-hindu-mythology-to-hollywood |work=[[Forbes]] |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261020013217/https://www.forbes.com/sites/yolarobert1/2024/05/18/film-industry-titan-brings-hindu-mythology-to-hollywood/ |archive-date=20 October 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |first=Sam |last=Davies |access-date=19 August 2026 |title=Mythical beasts, almighty gods, new technology: The epic blockbuster that could be India's answer to The Odyssey |url=https://www.bbc.com/culture/article/20260818-ramayana-the-epic-blockbuster-that-could-be-indias-answer-to-the-odyssey |work=[[BBC]] |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261021035853/https://www.bbc.com/culture/article/20260818-ramayana-the-epic-blockbuster-that-could-be-indias-answer-to-the-odyssey |archive-date=21 October 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> directed by [[Nitesh Tiwari]], who co-wrote the screenplay with [[Shridhar Raghavan]]. Produced by [[Namit Malhotra]] and [[Yash (actor)|Yash]],<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.ndtv.com/entertainment/yash-reveals-why-he-chose-to-co-produce-ramayana-with-namit-malhotra-12214958|title=Yash Reveals Why He Chose To Co-Produce Ramayana With Namit Malhotra|access-date=21 October 2026|website=NDTV|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261022082631/https://www.ndtv.com/entertainment/yash-reveals-why-he-chose-to-co-produce-ramayana-with-namit-malhotra-12214958|archive-date=22 October 2026|url-status=live}}</ref> the film is based on the Hindu epic ''[[Ramayana]]'' by [[Valmiki]]. It is the first of a two-part film, with ''Part 1'' being based on the first three ''kāṇḍa'' (chapters) of ''Ramayana'' which chronicles the life of Prince [[Rama]] from [[Balakanda|childhood]] up to his adventurous [[Ramayana#Araṇya Kāṇḍa|14-year exile]].<ref name=":2">{{Cite news |date=6 November 2024 |title=Ranbir Kapoor, Yash and Sai Pallavi's 'Ramayana Part 1 and 2' officially announced; first poster out |url=https://www.thehindu.com/entertainment/movies/ranbir-kapoor-yash-and-sai-pallavis-ramayana-part-1-and-2-officially-announced-first-poster-out/article68835920.ece |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241215233624/https://www.thehindu.com/entertainment/movies/ranbir-kapoor-yash-and-sai-pallavis-ramayana-part-1-and-2-officially-announced-first-poster-out/article68835920.ece |archive-date=15 December 2024 |access-date=31 March 2026 |work=The Hindu}}</ref><ref name=":3">{{Cite news |date=31 March 2026 |title='Ramayana' first glimpse: Ranbir Kapoor on playing Lord Ram: 'He is called Maryada Purushottam, which stands for an ideal man' – WATCH |url=https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/entertainment/hindi/bollywood/news/ramayana-first-glimpse-ranbir-kapoor-on-playing-lord-ram-he-is-called-maryada-purushottam-which-stands-for-an-ideal-man-watch/articleshow/129911188.cms |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260331034748/https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/entertainment/hindi/bollywood/news/ramayana-first-glimpse-ranbir-kapoor-on-playing-lord-ram-he-is-called-maryada-purushottam-which-stands-for-an-ideal-man-watch/articleshow/129911188.cms |archive-date=31 March 2026 |access-date=31 March 2026 |work=The Times of India}}</ref><ref name=":0">{{Cite web |date=19 August 2025 |title=Could this movie based on a Hindu epic become India's 'Avatar'? |url=https://www.latimes.com/entertainment-arts/business/newsletter/2025-08-19/could-this-movie-based-on-a-hindu-epic-become-indias-avatar |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250924230401/https://www.latimes.com/entertainment-arts/business/newsletter/2025-08-19/could-this-movie-based-on-a-hindu-epic-become-indias-avatar |archive-date=24 September 2025 |access-date=31 March 2026 |website=Los Angeles Times}}</ref> The first part features [[ensemble cast]] that includes [[Ranbir Kapoor]], Yash (in his Hindi film debut), [[Sai Pallavi]], [[Ravi Dubey]] (in his film debut), [[Anupam Kher]], [[Kajal Aggarwal]], [[Rakul Preet Singh]], [[Vivek Oberoi]], [[Kunal Kapoor (actor, born 1977)|Kunal Kapoor]], [[Adinath Kothare]], [[Arun Govil]], [[Indira Krishnan]], and [[Lara Dutta]].<ref name=":3" /><ref>{{Cite web |title=Ramayana full cast revealed: Full list of actors in Ranbir Kapoor's epic |url=https://www.business-standard.com/entertainment/ramayana-full-cast-revealed-full-list-of-actors-in-ranbir-kapoor-s-epic-nc-126073000830_1.html |access-date=30 July 2026 |website=Business Standard}}</ref>

The project was announced in May 2017 as a live-action adaptation of Valmiki's ''Ramayana'', initially conceived as a trilogy by producers; following several years of development and script refinement, it was restructured as a two-part film series under Tiwari's sole direction.<ref>{{cite news |title=Ramayana: Ranbir Kapoor-Yash-Sai Pallavi film's release date out, makers of Nitesh Tiwari's epic confirm two parts |url=https://indianexpress.com/article/entertainment/bollywood/ramayana-ranbir-kapoor-yash-sai-pallavi-films-release-date-out-makers-of-nitesh-tiwaris-epic-confirm-two-parts-9655800/ |work=The Indian Express |date=6 November 2024}}</ref>

