 an estimated combined budget of the duology being {{INRConvert|4000|c}}, it is the [[List of most expensive Indian films|most expensive Indian film]] ever made. It is also the [[List of most expensive non-English-language films|most expensive non-English language film]] ever made.<ref>{{cite news |title=Ranbir Kapoor-Yash starrer Ramayana to be India's costliest film ever at Rs 4000 crore, says producer Namit Malhotra |url=https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/entertainment/hindi/bollywood/news/ranbir-kapoor-yash-starrer-ramayana-to-be-indias-costliest-film-ever-at-rs-4000-crore-says-producer-namit-malhotra-were-funding-it-ourselves/articleshow/122463144.cms |work=The Times of India |date=15 July 2025 |access-date=30 March 2026 |archive-date=30 March 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260330092127/https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/entertainment/hindi/bollywood/news/ranbir-kapoor-yash-starrer-ramayana-to-be-indias-costliest-film-ever-at-rs-4000-crore-says-producer-namit-malhotra-were-funding-it-ourselves/articleshow/122463144.cms |url-status=live}}</ref>

