* [[Chetan Hansraj]] as [[List of characters in the Ramayana#S|Sumali]]
* [[Geeta Agarwal Sharma]] as [[Anusuya]]
}}

== Production ==
=== Origins ===
In May 2017, producers [[Allu Aravind]], Namit Malhotra, and [[Madhu Mantena]] announced their plans to collaborate and adapt the Hindu Sanskrit epic ''Ramayana'' into a [[Live action|live-action]] [[feature film]] [[trilogy]].<ref>{{cite news |access-date=11 May 2017 |title=Allu Aravind Announces Rs 500 Crore Ramayana After 1,000-Crore Mahabharata |url=https://www.ndtv.com/entertainment/allu-aravind-announces-rs-500-crore-ramayana-after-1-000-crore-mahabharata-1692105 |website=NDTV |archive-date=27 January 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210127195948/https://www.ndtv.com/entertainment/allu-aravind-announces-rs-500-crore-ramayana-after-1-000-crore-mahabharata-1692105 |url-status=live }}</ref> They revealed that the development of the script had already been underway for nearly a year. It was envisioned as a [[Multilingual film|multilingual production]] in [[Hindi]] along with several Indian regional languages and English. It was planned to be shot in [[3D film|3D]].<ref>{{Cite news |date=10 May 2017 |title='Ramayana' to be made into a movie of Rs 500 crore budget |url=https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/entertainment/telugu/movies/news/ramayana-to-be-made-into-a-movie-of-rs-500-crore-budget/articleshow/58611990.cms |access-date=17 February 2025 |work=The Times of India |issn=0971-8257 |archive-date=17 February 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250217094330/https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/entertainment/telugu/movies/news/ramayana-to-be-made-into-a-movie-of-rs-500-crore-budget/articleshow/58611990.cms |url-status=live }}</ref> Allu Aravind stated that his ambition was to bring ''Ramayana'' to the big screen in the "most magnificent way possible", while acknowledging that adapting the epic into a trilogy was an immense responsibility.<ref name="MM">{{cite web |first=Roshmila |last=Bhattacharya |access-date=10 May 2017 |title=Ramayana will now be a Rs 500-crore movie shot in three languages |url=https://mumbaimirror.indiatimes.com/entertainment/bollywood/ramayana-will-now-be-a-rs-500-crore-movie-shot-in-three-languages/articleshow/58602655.html |publisher=[[Mumbai Mirror]] |archive-date=3 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250703113730/https://mumbaimirror.indiatimes.com/entertainment/bollywood/ramayana-will-now-be-a-rs-500-crore-movie-shot-in-three-languages/articleshow/58602655.html |url-status=live }}</ref> Namit Malhotra, whose company Prime Focus had contributed visual effects to major [[Cinema of the United States|Hollywood]] films like ''[[Star Wars]]'', ''[[Transformers]]'', ''[[X-Men: Apocalypse]]'' and [[The Martian (film)|''The Martian'']] until then, saw in the trilogy the potential to set new global benchmarks for Indian cinema.<ref name="MM" /> In February 2018, Mantena revealed that his inspiration to make the film series came from the life and work of Indian comic book writer [[Anant Pai]], who had created the ''[[Amar Chitra Katha]]'' comics. He added that the film series was their collective effort in retelling Indian culture to newer generations in all possible "audio visual glory", with the help of the latest technology and visual effects.<ref>{{Cite web |date=23 February 2018 |title=Makers of Rs 500 crore Ramayana film sign MoU with UP government |url=https://indianexpress.com/article/entertainment/bollywood/ramayana-500-crore-film-mou-up-govt-5075106/ |access-date=17 February 2025 |website=The Indian Express |language=en |archive-date=17 February 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250217134114/https://indianexpress.com/article/entertainment/bollywood/ramayana-500-crore-film-mou-up-govt-5075106/ |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |date=21 February 2018 |title=MoUs worth Rs 4.28 lakh-crore signed on first day of UP Investors Summit 2018 |url=https://www.hindustantimes.com/lucknow/up-investors-summit-in-inaugural-session-industry-leaders-pledge-over-rs-88-000-cr-investment/story-LQE3NDTWVnFRyI2PRlmIgK.html |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230330010105/https://www.hindustantimes.com/lucknow/up-investors-summit-in-inaugural-session-industry-leaders-pledge-over-rs-88-000-cr-investment/story-LQE3NDTWVnFRyI2PRlmIgK.html |archive-date=30 March 2023 |access-date=16 March 2025 |work=Hindustan Times |language=en-us |url-status=live }}</ref> As the last widely recognised adaptations of the epic had been the television series,  [[Ramayan (1987 TV series)|''Ramayan'']] (1987–88) by [[Ramanand Sagar]], the producers stated that they wanted to adapt ''Ramayana'' for theatrical release.<ref>{{Cite web |date=10 May 2017 |title=Baahubali 2's success makes way for Rs 500-crore Ramayana film   |url=https://www.indiatoday.in/movies/regional-cinema/story/baahubali-2-the-conclusion-ramayana-film-500-crore-976236-2017-05-10 |access-date=17 February 2025 |website=India Today |language=en |archive-date=17 February 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250217094330/https://www.indiatoday.in/movies/regional-cinema/story/baahubali-2-the-conclusion-ramayana-film-500-crore-976236-2017-05-10 |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Hingorani |first=Karishma |date=10 May 2017 |title=Now Gear up for a Rs 500-Crore 3D 'Ramayana' on the Big Screen |url=https://www.thequint.com/entertainment/cinema/500-crore-ramayana-film-in-3-languages#read-more |access-date=17 February 2025 |website=TheQuint |language=en |archive-date=26 April 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250426123605/https://www.thequint.com/entertainment/cinema/500-crore-ramayana-film-in-3-languages#read-more |url-status=live }}</ref>

=== Development ===

{{Multiple image
| image1      = The Director Nitesh Tiwari of the film DANGAL at the Master Class, during the 48th International Film Festival of India (IFFI-2017), in Panaji, Goa on November 23, 2017.jpg
| image2      = Namit Malhotra (cropped).jpg
| total_width = 400px
| footer      = ''Ramayana'' is the first collaboration of [[Nitesh Tiwari]] and [[Namit Malhotra]].
}}

In July 2019, Tiwari and Ravi Udyawar came on board to co-direct the trilogy, while Shridhar Raghavan was hired to write the screenplay.<ref>{{Cite web |date=8 July 2019 |title=Ramayana's trilingual live-action trilogy to be helmed by Dangal director Nitesh Tiwari, Ravi Udyawar |url=https://www.firstpost.com/entertainment/ramayanas-trilingual-live-action-trilogy-to-be-helmed-by-dangal-director-nitesh-tiwari-ravi-udyawar-6953121.html |access-date=17 February 2025 |website=Firstpost |language=en-us}}</ref> Tiwari and Udyawar said they were motivated to undertake the project out of a sense of responsibility toward introducing the epic to their children, who, according to Tiwari, were familiar with the broad outline of the Ramayana but had not engaged with it in depth. Tiwari further cited the significant advancements in visual effects since the 1987–88 ''[[Ramayan (1987 TV series)|Ramayan]]'' television series as another factor behind the project.<ref name=":19" /> The producers' planned to commence filming by 2020 and maintain a relatively short gap between the release of each part. The first instalment was scheduled to be released in 2021.<ref name=":6">{{Cite news |date=8 July 2019 |title=Nitesh Tiwari, Ravi Udyawar to bring 'Ramayana' to life at a Rs 500 crore budget |url=https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/magazines/panache/nitesh-tiwari-ravi-udyawar-to-bring-ramayana-to-life-at-a-rs-500-crore-budget/articleshow/70126241.cms?from=mdr |access-date=24 July 2025 |work=The Economic Times |issn=0013-0389}}</ref> The production team commissioned paintings by artists from across India to serve as references for the films' settings, costumes, character designs and action sequences. The project also aimed to cast actors from different regional film industries to appeal to pan-Indian and international audiences.<ref name=":19">{{Cite news |date=8 July 2019 |author=Roshmila Bhattacharya |title=Nitesh Tiwari, Ravi Udyawar reviving Ramayana with a live-action, multilingual trilogy |url=https://mumbaimirror.indiatimes.com/entertainment/bollywood/nitesh-tiwari-ravi-udyawar-reviving-ramayana-with-a-live-action-multilingual-trilogy/articleshow/70119460.cms |access-date=17 February 2025 |newspaper=Mumbai Mirror |language=en |archive-date=17 February 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250217094330/https://mumbaimirror.indiatimes.com/entertainment/bollywood/nitesh-tiwari-ravi-udyawar-reviving-ramayana-with-a-live-action-multilingual-trilogy/articleshow/70119460.cms |url-status=live }}</ref>

=== Pre-production ===
In November 2019, Tiwari said that Raghavan had been writing the screenplay for the past three years under the guidance of scholars and [[Pandit|''pandits'']] with expertise in the scriptures and epic, to ensure that the adaptation remained culturally accurate while making it accessible to contemporary audiences.<ref name=":7">{{Cite news |date=20 November 2019 |title=I'm happy not following the formula of making a hit film: Nitesh Tiwari |url=https://www.hindustantimes.com/bollywood/i-m-happy-not-following-the-formula-of-making-a-hit-film-nitesh-tiwari/story-X7ojYtj4L7MBKe5PMoMleP.html |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240725202209/https://www.hindustantimes.com/bollywood/i-m-happy-not-following-the-formula-of-making-a-hit-film-nitesh-tiwari/story-X7ojYtj4L7MBKe5PMoMleP.html |archive-date=25 July 2024 |access-date=15 March 2025 |work=Hindustan Times |language=en-us |url-status=live }}</ref> In April 2020, Tiwari stated that they were carefully identifying aspects of the story that should remain unchanged while determining where limited cinematic liberties could be taken without affecting the epic's cultural and religious significance.<ref name=":8">{{Cite web |date=12 October 2019 |title=Massive responsibility to do a project like Ramayana: Nitesh Tiwari |url=https://indianexpress.com/article/entertainment/bollywood/massive-responsibility-to-do-a-project-like-ramayana-nitesh-tiwari-6066033/ |access-date=18 February 2025 |website=The Indian Express |language=en |archive-date=3 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250703113725/https://indianexpress.com/article/entertainment/bollywood/massive-responsibility-to-do-a-project-like-ramayana-nitesh-tiwari-6066033/ |url-status=live }}</ref> Tiwari further added that the team sought to make the film appealing to younger audiences while remaining faithful to the expectations of audiences familiar with traditional retellings. He also described the project as technologically demanding because of its extensive visual effects requirements, citing the epic's fantastical settings and creatures as presenting opportunities for large-scale world-building.<ref>{{Cite web |date=5 March 2020 |title=Challenging to make Ramayana appealing for all generations: Nitesh Tiwari |url=https://indianexpress.com/article/entertainment/bollywood/challenging-to-make-ramayana-appealing-for-all-generations-nitesh-tiwari-6300240/ |access-date=17 February 2025 |website=The Indian Express |language=en |archive-date=26 April 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250426123456/https://indianexpress.com/article/entertainment/bollywood/challenging-to-make-ramayana-appealing-for-all-generations-nitesh-tiwari-6300240/ |url-status=live }}</ref><ref name=":9">{{Cite web |date=5 March 2020 |title=Nitesh Tiwari on Ramayana: Making it exciting for both children and old people is challenging |url=https://www.indiatoday.in/movies/bollywood/story/nitesh-tiwari-on-ramayana-making-it-exciting-for-both-children-and-old-people-is-challenging-1652718-2020-03-05 |access-date=17 February 2025 |website=India Today |language=en}}</ref> During the [[COVID-19 pandemic in India]], the development of screenplay continued through virtual meetings involving members of the creative team across the country.<ref name=":10">{{Cite news |date=31 March 2020 |title=Amid the lockdown, Nitesh Tiwari works on Ramayana's script over group calls |url=https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/entertainment/hindi/bollywood/news/amid-the-lockdown-nitesh-tiwari-works-on-ramayanas-script-over-group-calls/articleshow/74919720.cms |access-date=17 February 2025 |work=The Times of India |issn=0971-8257 |archive-date=17 February 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250217134113/https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/entertainment/hindi/bollywood/news/amid-the-lockdown-nitesh-tiwari-works-on-ramayanas-script-over-group-calls/articleshow/74919720.cms |url-status=live }}</ref>

In June 2021, Mantena said that the trilogy was being developed as a long-term project, revealing that more than 200 artists from around the world, including several [[Academy Awards|Academy Award]] winners, had been working on it for two years using a production process inspired by [[Avatar (franchise)|''Avatar'']].<ref name=":11">{{Cite web |last=Hymavati |first=Ravali |date=30 June 2021 |title=Madhu Mantena Opens Up On Ramayana And Says, 'Expect The Biggest Cast In History Of Indian Cinema' |url=https://www.thehansindia.com/cinema/bollywood/madhu-mantena-opens-up-on-ramayana-and-says-expect-the-biggest-cast-in-history-of-indian-cinema-693416 |access-date=17 February 2025 |website=www.thehansindia.com |language=en |archive-date=17 February 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250217134114/https://www.thehansindia.com/cinema/bollywood/madhu-mantena-opens-up-on-ramayana-and-says-expect-the-biggest-cast-in-history-of-indian-cinema-693416 |url-status=live }}</ref> The following month, he described the trilogy as a linear adaptation of Valmiki's ''Ramayana'' that would incorporate many of the epic's subsidiary narratives while extensive digital assets were being created during pre-production. In September 2021, Mantena said that the filmmakers were primarily drawing from Valmiki's ''Ramayana'' while also studying artistic interpretations by painters such as [[Raja Ravi Varma]], emphasising that the project was intended to be a traditional adaptation rather than a reinterpretation of the epic.<ref>{{Cite web |last1=Bhasin |first1=Shriya |date=2 July 2021 |title='Ramayana' trilogy for a global audience but rooted in India, says producer Madhu Mantena |url=https://www.indiatvnews.com/entertainment/celebrities/ramayana-trilogy-for-a-global-audience-but-rooted-in-india-says-producer-madhu-mantena-716208 |access-date=15 March 2025 |website=India TV News |language=en |archive-date=26 April 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250426123450/https://www.indiatvnews.com/entertainment/celebrities/ramayana-trilogy-for-a-global-audience-but-rooted-in-india-says-producer-madhu-mantena-716208 |url-status=live }}</ref> In December 2022, Mantena said that the screenplay was expected to be completed within a few months, with principal photography planned to begin in September 2023.<ref>{{Cite news |date=4 December 2022 |title=Madhu Mantena reveals 'Ramayana' shooting will start from September 2023 |url=https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/entertainment/hindi/bollywood/news/madhu-mantena-reveals-ramayana-shooting-will-start-from-september-2023/articleshow/95975114.cms |access-date=24 July 2025 |work=The Times of India |issn=0971-8257 |archive-date=18 February 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250218140919/https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/entertainment/hindi/bollywood/news/madhu-mantena-reveals-ramayana-shooting-will-start-from-september-2023/articleshow/95975114.cms |url-status=live }}</ref> In June 2023, he dismissed reports that the project had been indefinitely postponed, stating that filming was expected to begin later that year.<ref>{{Cite news |date=7 June 2023 |title=Producer Madhu Mantena rubbishes reports of Ramayan's indefinite postponement |url=https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/entertainment/hindi/bollywood/news/producer-madhu-mantena-rubbishes-reports-of-ramayans-indefinite-postponement/articleshow/100823158.cms |access-date=24 July 2025 |work=The Times of India |issn=0971-8257}}</ref> In March 2024, it was reported that [[DNEG]] virtual production had come on board as the producer alongside Mantena.<ref>{{cite web |access-date=13 March 2024 |title=Ranbir Kapoor's Ramayana rights acquired by Namit Malhotra |url=https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/entertainment/hindi/bollywood/news/ranbir-kapoors-ramayana-to-be-backed-by-namit-malhotra/articleshow/108459580.cms |website=The Times of India |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260929052242/https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/entertainment/hindi/bollywood/news/ranbir-kapoors-ramayana-to-be-backed-by-namit-malhotra/articleshow/108459580.cms |archive-date=29 September 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |date=28 March 2024 |title=Madhu Mantena backs out as producer from Nitesh Tiwari's Ramayana due to monetary concerns; details inside |url=https://www.hindustantimes.com/htcity/cinema/madhu-mantena-backs-out-as-producer-from-nitesh-tiwaris-ramayana-due-to-monetary-concerns-details-inside-101711520764418.html |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240617222651/https://www.hindustantimes.com/htcity/cinema/madhu-mantena-backs-out-as-producer-from-nitesh-tiwaris-ramayana-due-to-monetary-concerns-details-inside-101711520764418.html |archive-date=17 June 2024 |access-date=24 July 2025 |work=Hindustan Times |language=en-us |url-status=live }}</ref> In the same month, it was reported that Mantena had stepped back from his role as a producer citing financial concerns.<ref>{{cite web |access-date=16 March 2024 |title=Ranbir Kapoor's Ramayana faces trouble as producer Madhu Mantena backs out: Report |url=https://www.firstpost.com/entertainment/ranbir-kapoors-ramayana-faces-trouble-as-producer-madhu-mantena-backs-out-report-13749490.html |website=Firstpost}}</ref> He later got involved in a legal tussle with Malhotra's Prime Focus Technologies regarding the IP rights of the film, which was ultimately settled when he was provided compensation of ₹80 crore.<ref>{{Cite news |date=3 April 2024 |title=Has Madhu Mantena exited the Ramayana franchise for good? Here's the full story: Exclusive! |url=https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/entertainment/hindi/bollywood/news/has-madhu-mantena-exited-the-ramayana-franchise-for-good-heres-the-full-story-exclusive/articleshow/109001133.cms |access-date=24 July 2025 |work=The Times of India |issn=0971-8257 |archive-date=24 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250724230240/https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/entertainment/hindi/bollywood/news/has-madhu-mantena-exited-the-ramayana-franchise-for-good-heres-the-full-story-exclusive/articleshow/109001133.cms |url-status=live }}</ref> Later, in April 2024, it was confirmed that [[Yash (actor)|Yash]] through his company ''Monster Mind Creations'' was co-producing the film alongside Malhotra.<ref>{{cite web |access-date=12 April 2024 |title=KGF Star Yash To Produce Ramayana With Namit Malhotra |url=https://www.ndtv.com/entertainment/kgf-star-yash-to-produce-nitesh-tiwaris-ramayana-with-namit-malhotra-5425677 |website=NDTV |archive-date=12 April 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240412093457/https://www.ndtv.com/entertainment/kgf-star-yash-to-produce-nitesh-tiwaris-ramayana-with-namit-malhotra-5425677 |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |access-date=12 April 2024 |title=Yash to co-produce and act in Nitesh Tiwari-Ranbir Kapoor's 'Ramayana' |url=https://www.indiatoday.in/movies/celebrities/story/yash-to-co-produce-and-act-in-nitesh-tiwari-ranbir-kapoors-ramayana-2526352-2024-04-12 |website=India Today |archive-date=16 April 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240416111621/https://www.indiatoday.in/movies/celebrities/story/yash-to-co-produce-and-act-in-nitesh-tiwari-ranbir-kapoors-ramayana-2526352-2024-04-12 |url-status=live }}</ref>

