In July 2021, Mantena said that the ensemble cast would be announced by Diwali later that year.<ref>{{Cite web |access-date=1 July 2021 |title=Deepika Padukone's Draupadi will take off after Ramayana, Madhu Mantena reveals |url=https://www.indiatoday.in/movies/celebrities/story/deepika-padukone-s-draupadi-will-take-off-after-ramayana-madhu-mantena-reveals-1821663-2021-07-01 |website=India Today |language=en |archive-date=1 July 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210701120046/https://www.indiatoday.in/movies/celebrities/story/deepika-padukone-s-draupadi-will-take-off-after-ramayana-madhu-mantena-reveals-1821663-2021-07-01 |url-status=live }}</ref> He stated that the film would feature what he described as "the biggest cast ever in the history of Indian cinema" and that actors would be drawn from across the country, saying the casting reflected the filmmakers' intention to present the epic as a [[Pan-Indian film|pan-Indian project]].<ref name=":11" /> [[Mukesh Chhabra]] was announced as the casting director for the film.<ref>{{Cite web |title=When Mukesh Chhabra revealed why he cast Ranbir Kapoor as Ram in Nitesh Tiwari's Ramayana |url=https://www.hindustantimes.com/entertainment/bollywood/when-mukesh-chhabra-revealed-why-he-cast-ranbir-kapoor-as-ram-in-nitesh-tiwaris-ramayana-101752057188323.html |access-date=9 July 2025 |website=[[Hindustan Times]] |archive-date=1 August 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260801021031/https://www.hindustantimes.com/entertainment/bollywood/when-mukesh-chhabra-revealed-why-he-cast-ranbir-kapoor-as-ram-in-nitesh-tiwaris-ramayana-101752057188323.html |url-status=live }}</ref> In August 2023, [[Ranbir Kapoor]] and [[Yash (actor)|Yash]] joined the film for the roles of Rama and Ravana respectively.<ref>{{cite web |access-date=23 August 2023 |title=Exclusive: Yash undergoes look test for Ramayana, Ranbir Kapoor's speculation for the role of Rama is true |url=https://www.bollywoodhungama.com/news/bollywood/exclusive-yash-undergoes-look-test-ramayana-ranbir-kapoors-speculation-role-rama-true |website=Bollywood Hungama |archive-date=23 August 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230823163530/https://www.bollywoodhungama.com/news/bollywood/exclusive-yash-undergoes-look-test-ramayana-ranbir-kapoors-speculation-role-rama-true/ |url-status=live }}</ref> Later, Kapoor was confirmed to play dual role of Rama as well as Parashurama.<ref>{{cite web |access-date=4 April 2026 |title=Ranbir Kapoor opens up on playing both Lord Rama and Parashurama in Ramayana: "It was fantastic" |url=https://www.bollywoodhungama.com/news/bollywood/ranbir-kapoor-opens-playing-lord-rama-parashurama-ramayana-fantastic/ |website=Bollywood Hungama |archive-date=4 April 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260404092316/https://www.bollywoodhungama.com/news/bollywood/ranbir-kapoor-opens-playing-lord-rama-parashurama-ramayana-fantastic/ |url-status=live }}</ref> In the same month [[Sai Pallavi]] joined the cast for the role of Sita.<ref>{{cite web |access-date=24 August 2023 |title=Sai Pallavi to likely play female lead in Nitesh Tiwari's Ramayana: Report |url=https://www.bollywoodhungama.com/news/bollywood/sai-pallavi-likely-play-female-lead-nitesh-tiwaris-ramayana-report/ |website=Bollywood Hungama |archive-date=24 August 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230824134407/https://www.bollywoodhungama.com/news/bollywood/sai-pallavi-likely-play-female-lead-nitesh-tiwaris-ramayana-report/ |url-status=live }}</ref> In October 2023, [[Sunny Deol]] also joined the cast for the role of Hanuman. He reportedly charged ₹45 crore for his role.<ref>{{cite web |access-date=26 October 2023 |title=Sunny Deol's Fees For Nitesh Tiwari's Ramayana Will Be A WHOPPING Rs 45 Crores? Know Here |url=https://www.news18.com/movies/sunny-deols-fees-for-nitesh-tiwaris-ramayana-will-be-a-whopping-rs-45-crores-know-here-8635345.html |website=News18 |archive-date=26 October 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231026231426/https://www.news18.com/movies/sunny-deols-fees-for-nitesh-tiwaris-ramayana-will-be-a-whopping-rs-45-crores-know-here-8635345.html |url-status=live }}</ref> In early 2024, [[Vijay Sethupathi]] was rumoured to play the role of Vibhishana in the film,<ref>{{cite web |access-date=26 January 2024 |title=Vijay Sethupathi could be seen as Vibhishan in Ranbir Kapoor's Ramayan: Report |url=https://www.hindustantimes.com/entertainment/bollywood/vijay-sethupathi-vibhishan-ranbir-kapoor-ramayan-report-101706259395107.html |website=Hindustan Times |archive-date=26 January 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240126101237/https://www.hindustantimes.com/entertainment/bollywood/vijay-sethupathi-vibhishan-ranbir-kapoor-ramayan-report-101706259395107.html |url-status=live }}</ref> however later he declined these rumours.<ref>{{cite web |access-date=9 February 2026 |title=Vijay Sethupathi Clarifies He Is Not Part Of Nitesh Tiwari's Ramayana |url=https://www.filmfare.com/news/bollywood/vijay-sethupathi-clarifies-he-is-not-part-of-nitesh-tiwaris-ramayana-81585.html |website=Filmfare |archive-date=9 February 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260209150840/https://www.filmfare.com/news/bollywood/vijay-sethupathi-clarifies-he-is-not-part-of-nitesh-tiwaris-ramayana-81585.html |url-status=live }}</ref> Similarly, [[Bobby Deol]] was also reportedly rumoured to play the role of Kumbhakarna which also turned false.<ref>{{cite web |access-date=16 January 2024 |title=Bobby Deol NOT cast in Nitesh Tiwari's Ramayana, confirms actor's team |url=https://www.bollywoodhungama.com/news/bollywood/bobby-deol-not-cast-nitesh-tiwaris-ramayana-confirms-actors-team/ |website=Bollywood Hungama |archive-date=16 January 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240116123915/https://www.bollywoodhungama.com/news/bollywood/bobby-deol-not-cast-nitesh-tiwaris-ramayana-confirms-actors-team/ |url-status=live }}</ref> In February 2024, [[Rakul Preet Singh]] reportedly joined the cast for the role of Shurpanakha.<ref>{{cite web |access-date=10 February 2024 |title=Rakul Preet Singh in talks to play Shurpanakha in Ranbir Kapoor – Nitesh Tiwari's Ramayana? Here's what we know |url=https://www.bollywoodhungama.com/news/bollywood/rakul-preet-singh-talks-play-shurpanakha-ranbir-kapoor-nitesh-tiwaris-ramayana-heres-know/ |website=Bollywood Hungama}}</ref> In March 2024, [[Ravi Dubey]] also reportedly joined the film for the role of Lakshmana.<ref>{{cite web |access-date=22 March 2024 |title=Ravi Dubey To Play Lakshman In Ranbir Kapoor's Ramayan: Report |url=https://www.ndtv.com/entertainment/ranbir-kapoor-s-ramayan-gets-a-lakshman-in-ravi-dubey-reports-5290343 |website=NDTV |archive-date=22 March 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240322124943/https://www.ndtv.com/entertainment/ranbir-kapoor-s-ramayan-gets-a-lakshman-in-ravi-dubey-reports-5290343 |url-status=live }}</ref> In April 2024, [[Arun Govil]], [[Lara Dutta]] and [[Sheeba Chaddha]] were also confirmed to be part of the film after images leaked from the sets confirmed their presence.<ref name="NDTVSets2024">{{cite web |title=Crazy Viral Pics Of Lara Dutta And Arun Govil From The Sets Of Nitesh Tiwari's Ramayana |url=https://www.ndtv.com/entertainment/crazy-viral-pics-of-lara-dutta-and-arjun-govil-from-the-sets-of-nitesh-tiwaris-ramayana-5379317 |access-date=19 February 2025 |website=NDTV |language=en |archive-date=3 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250703113725/https://www.ndtv.com/entertainment/crazy-viral-pics-of-lara-dutta-and-arjun-govil-from-the-sets-of-nitesh-tiwaris-ramayana-5379317 |url-status=live}}</ref> In July 2024, [[Kunal Kapoor (actor, born 1977)|Kunal Kapoor]] was confirmed to play an important role in the film.<ref>{{cite web |access-date=30 July 2024 |title=Kunal Kapoor joins cast of Ranbir Kapoor, Nitesh Tiwari's epic Ramayana; begins prep for role: Report |url=https://www.bollywoodhungama.com/news/bollywood/kunal-kapoor-joins-cast-ranbir-kapoor-nitesh-tiwaris-epic-ramayana-begins-prep-role-report |website=Bollywood Hungama |archive-date=30 July 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240730122430/https://www.bollywoodhungama.com/news/bollywood/kunal-kapoor-joins-cast-ranbir-kapoor-nitesh-tiwaris-epic-ramayana-begins-prep-role-report/ |url-status=live }}</ref> In September 2024, [[Indira Krishnan]] also the joined the cast.<ref>{{cite web |access-date=18 September 2024 |title=Indira Krishnan calls Ramayana co-star Ranbir Kapoor 'one of the finest actors', shares warm moments from film's set |url=https://www.bollywoodhungama.com/news/features/indira-krishnan-calls-ramayana-co-star-ranbir-kapoor-one-finest-actors-shares-warm-moments-films-set |website=Bollywood Hungama |archive-date=18 September 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240918153622/https://www.bollywoodhungama.com/news/features/indira-krishnan-calls-ramayana-co-star-ranbir-kapoor-one-finest-actors-shares-warm-moments-films-set/ |url-status=live }}</ref> In May 2025, [[Kajal Aggarwal]] joined the cast for the role of Mandodari.<ref>{{cite web |access-date=16 May 2025 |title=Kajal Aggarwal joins Nitesh Tiwari's Ramayana as Mandodari opposite Yash's Ravana |url=https://www.hindustantimes.com/entertainment/bollywood/kajal-aggarwal-joins-nitesh-tiwaris-ramayana-as-mandodari-opposite-yashs-ravana-101747392220286.html |website=Hindustan Times |archive-date=16 May 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250516163344/https://www.hindustantimes.com/entertainment/bollywood/kajal-aggarwal-joins-nitesh-tiwaris-ramayana-as-mandodari-opposite-yashs-ravana-101747392220286.html |url-status=live }}</ref> [[Vivek Oberoi]] joined the cast in June 2025<ref>{{cite web |access-date=7 June 2025 |title=Vivek Oberoi Joins Nitesh Tiwari's Ramayana |url=https://www.news18.com/movies/bollywood/vivek-oberoi-joins-nitesh-tiwaris-ramayana-take-a-look-at-full-cast-ws-l-9373870.html |website=News18 |archive-date=7 June 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250607131143/https://www.news18.com/movies/bollywood/vivek-oberoi-joins-nitesh-tiwaris-ramayana-take-a-look-at-full-cast-ws-l-9373870.html |url-status=live }}</ref> while [[Adinath Kothare]] and [[Shobana]] joined the cast in July 2025.<ref>{{cite web |access-date=23 July 2025 |title=Exclusive: Addinath Kothare CONFIRMS playing Bharat in Ramayana; says, "It is one of the FINEST scripts I have read" |url=https://www.bollywoodhungama.com/news/features/exclusive-addinath-kothare-confirms-playing-bharat-ramayana-says-one-finest-scripts-read/ |website=Bollywood Hungama |archive-date=23 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250723073417/https://www.bollywoodhungama.com/news/features/exclusive-addinath-kothare-confirms-playing-bharat-ramayana-says-one-finest-scripts-read/ |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |access-date=4 July 2025 |title=Shobana To Play Ravana's Mother Kaikasi In Ranbir Kapoor's Ramayana |url=https://www.news18.com/movies/bollywood/shobana-to-play-ravanas-mother-kaikasi-in-ranbir-kapoors-ramayana-9421313.html |website=News18 |archive-date=4 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250704132430/https://www.news18.com/movies/bollywood/shobana-to-play-ravanas-mother-kaikasi-in-ranbir-kapoors-ramayana-9421313.html |url-status=live }}</ref> [[Amitabh Bachchan]] was initially rumoured to voice the character of [[Jatayu]], however [[Anupam Kher]] was later confirmed to be cast instead.<ref>{{cite web |access-date=21 July 2026 |title=Ramayana: Anupam Kher roped in as Jatayu's voice, Amitabh Bachchan rumours put to rest |url=https://indianexpress.com/article/entertainment/bollywood/ramayana-anupam-kher-roped-in-as-jatayus-voice-amitabh-bachchan-rumours-put-to-rest-10796540 |website=The Indian Express |archive-date=21 July 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260721105130/https://indianexpress.com/article/entertainment/bollywood/ramayana-anupam-kher-roped-in-as-jatayus-voice-amitabh-bachchan-rumours-put-to-rest-10796540/ |url-status=live }}</ref> In March 2026, [[Faisal Malik]] was confirmed to play the role of Kumbhakarna.<ref>{{cite web |access-date=16 March 2026 |title='Ramayana': 'Panchayat' star Faisal Malik bags the role of Kumbhakarna in Ranbir Kapoor starrer magnum opus - Reports |url=https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/entertainment/hindi/bollywood/news/ramayana-panchayat-star-faisal-malik-bags-the-role-of-kumbhakarna-in-ranbir-kapoor-starrer-magnum-opus-reports/articleshow/129602656.cms |website=The Times of India |archive-date=16 March 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260316072301/https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/entertainment/hindi/bollywood/news/ramayana-panchayat-star-faisal-malik-bags-the-role-of-kumbhakarna-in-ranbir-kapoor-starrer-magnum-opus-reports/articleshow/129602656.cms |url-status=live }}</ref> [[Harish Uthaman]] reportedly joined the cast for the role of Vibhishana while [[Raghav Juyal]] was  reported to play the role of [[Indrajit|Meghanada]].<ref>{{cite web |access-date=31 July 2026 |title=Ramayana: Hanuman To Vibhishan, Characters Missing From Trailer And Actors Playing Them |url=https://www.timesnownews.com/entertainment-news/bollywood/ramayana-hanuman-to-vibhishan-characters-missing-from-trailer-and-actors-playing-them-article-155222744 |website=Times Now |archive-date=1 August 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260801015702/https://www.timesnownews.com/entertainment-news/bollywood/ramayana-hanuman-to-vibhishan-characters-missing-from-trailer-and-actors-playing-them-article-155222744 |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |date=7 February 2026 |title=Raghav Juyal cast as Meghanad in Ranbir Kapoor's Ramayana after Vikrant Massey's exit |url=https://indianexpress.com/article/entertainment/bollywood/raghav-juyal-cast-as-meghanad-in-ranbir-kapoors-ramayana-after-vikrant-masseys-exit-10519517/lite |work=The Indian Express |access-date=1 November 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260210200755/https://indianexpress.com/article/entertainment/bollywood/raghav-juyal-cast-as-meghanad-in-ranbir-kapoors-ramayana-after-vikrant-masseys-exit-10519517/lite/ |archive-date=10 February 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> 

Originally, Yash and Sai Pallavi's own voices for [[Ravana]] and [[Sita]] were used in the first official Hindi trailer of the film, respectively. However, since neither actor is a native Hindi speaker, their dialogues attracted attention from viewers. Yash's pronunciation and vocal impact as Ravana was criticised,<ref>{{cite news |date=30 July 2026 |title=Yash wins praise as Ravana in 'Ramayana' trailer, but Hindi voice draws mixed reactions– Report |url=https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/entertainment/hindi/bollywood/news/yash-wins-praise-as-ravana-in-ramayana-trailer-but-hindi-voice-draws-mixed-reactions-report/articleshow/132736937.cms |access-date=8 November 2026 |work=The Times of India}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=2026-07-30 |title='Ramayana' trailer Twitter review: 'Yash is going to get loudest cheers,' say users on Ranbir Kapoor's upcoming film - BusinessToday |url=https://www.businesstoday.in/trending/entertainment/story/ramayana-trailer-twitter-review-yash-is-going-to-get-loudest-cheers-say-users-on-ranbir-kapoors-upcoming-film-546143-2026-07-30 |access-date=2026-11-08 |website=Business Today |language=en}}</ref> while Sai Pallavi's Hindi received mixed responses.<ref>{{Cite web |last= |first= |date=2026-07-30 |title=Ramayana trailer: Ranbir's Ram, Yash's Raavan stand at heart of a cinematic odyssey |url=https://www.indiatoday.in/movies/bollywood/story/ramayana-trailer-ranbir-kapoor-ram-yash-raavan-stand-at-heart-of-a-cinematic-odyssey-2959376-2026-07-30 |access-date=2026-11-08 |website=India Today |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last=Rani |first=Gayatri |date=30 July 2026 |title=Ramayana trailer out: Ranbir Kapoor’s divine Ram faces Yash’s fearsome Raavan in an epic showdown |url=https://www.moneycontrol.com/entertainment/ramayana-trailer-out-ranbir-kapoor-s-lord-rama-sai-pallavi-as-sita-yash-s-ravana-makes-powerful-entry-article-13987660.html |access-date=8 November 2026 |work=Moneycontrol}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Keshri |first=Shweta |date=2026-07-31 |title=Sai Pallavi as Sita: Beauty debate erupts after Ramayana trailer |url=https://www.indiatoday.in/movies/bollywood/story/ramayana-trailer-sai-pallavi-as-sita-sparks-debate-over-beauty-standards-2960331-2026-07-31 |access-date=2026-11-08 |website=India Today |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Ramayana: Sonia Balani says Sai Pallavi has improved a lot amid Hindi accent trolling |url=https://www.mid-day.com/entertainment/bollywood-news/article/exclusive-ramayana-actor-sonia-balani-reveals-ranbir-kapoor-transformed-into-lord-rama-within-10-days-23649917 |access-date=2026-11-08 |website=Mid-Day}}</ref> The second Hindi trailer featured a new voiceover for Ravana<ref>{{cite news |date=16 October 2026 |title=‘Ramayana Rise of a Legend’ NEW Hindi trailer features new voiceover for Yash as Ravana alongside Ranbir Kapoor as Lord Ram, netizens praise improved visuals and fight sequence |url=https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/articleshow/134992957.cms |access-date=8 November 2026 |work=The Times of India}}</ref>, with [[Sharad Kelkar]] subsequently confirming that he dubbed Yash's Hindi dialogue. Kelkar explained that the filmmakers' decision to dub over Yash was due to his Kannada accent affecting the rhythm of his Hindi dialogues. Yash nonetheless dubbed his own dialogues in the Kannada dub.<ref>{{cite news |last=Banerjee |first=Urmimala |date=6 November 2026 |title=Sharad Kelkar On Dubbing For Yash in ‘Ramayana’: ‘We Were All In Sync’ (EXCLUSIVE) |url=https://varietyindia.com/sharad-kelkar-on-dubbing-for-yash-in-ramayana-we-were-all-in-sync-exclusive/ |access-date=8 November 2026 |work=Variety India}}</ref> [[Ami Trivedi]] provided Pallavi's Hindi voice, consulting the actress and matching the emotional nuances of her performance.<ref>{{cite news |author=Srijani Roy Chowdhury |date=6 November 2026 |title=‘Ramayana: Part 1’: Ami Trivedi on Dubbing for Sai Pallavi, Recreating Her Voice and the Ayodhya Exit Scene (EXCLUSIVE) |url=https://varietyindia.com/ramayana-part-1-ami-trivedi-on-dubbing-for-sai-pallavi-recreating-her-voice-and-the-ayodhya-exit-scene-exclusive/ |access-date=8 November 2026 |work=Variety India}}</ref>

=== Filming ===
In January 2024, reports indicated that Kapoor and Pallavi were expected to begin filming in March, with dialogue-heavy scenes scheduled first, followed by large-scale crowd and battle sequences.<ref>{{Cite web |date=12 January 2024 |title=Ranbir Kapoor to start shooting for Nitesh Tiwari's 'Ramayan' in March |url=https://www.mid-day.com/entertainment/bollywood-news/article/sai-pallavi-yash-ranbir-kapoor-to-start-shoot-for-nitesh-tiwaris-ramayan-in-march-23329464 |access-date=24 July 2025 |website=Mid-day |language=en |archive-date=24 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250724230155/https://www.mid-day.com/entertainment/bollywood-news/article/sai-pallavi-yash-ranbir-kapoor-to-start-shoot-for-nitesh-tiwaris-ramayan-in-march-23329464 |url-status=live }}</ref> In March, filming was reportedly postponed to April to allow additional time for the completion of costumes and production design.<ref>{{Cite web |date=15 March 2024 |title=Ranbir Kapoor-starrer Ramayana, which was to roll this month, pushed to mid-April as epic drama's outfits are being reworked |url=https://www.mid-day.com/entertainment/bollywood-news/article/ranbir-kapoor-starrer-ramayana-which-was-to-roll-this-month-pushed-to-mid-april-as-epic-drama-outfits-are-being-reworked-23339922 |access-date=24 July 2025 |website=Mid-day |language=en |archive-date=24 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250724230155/https://www.mid-day.com/entertainment/bollywood-news/article/ranbir-kapoor-starrer-ramayana-which-was-to-roll-this-month-pushed-to-mid-april-as-epic-drama-outfits-are-being-reworked-23339922 |url-status=live }}</ref> [[Principal photography]] for the first part began on 2 April, in [[Film City, Mumbai]], under the [[working title]] ''God Power''. The opening schedule featured ''[[gurukula]]'' sequences involving the child actors portraying the four princes of [[Ayodhya (Ramayana)|Ayodhya]] and [[Shishir Sharma]] as [[Vasishtha]], with a specially constructed [[Ayodhya]] set serving as the primary filming location.<ref>{{Cite web |date=5 April 2024 |title=Ranbir Kapoor's Ramayana Shoot Begins, FIRST Video of Grand Ayodhya Set Goes Viral |url=https://www.news18.com/movies/ranbir-kapoor-ramayana-shoot-begins-first-video-of-grand-ayodhya-set-goes-viral-8840316.html |access-date=7 November 2024 |website=News18 |archive-date=3 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250703113725/https://www.news18.com/movies/ranbir-kapoor-ramayana-shoot-begins-first-video-of-grand-ayodhya-set-goes-viral-8840316.html |url-status=live }}</ref><ref name=":12">{{Cite news |date=17 May 2024 |title=Ranbir Kapoor-starrer Ramayana's working title revealed; makers tightens surveillance on set to avoid leaked pics |url=https://www.hindustantimes.com/entertainment/bollywood/ranbir-kapoor-ramayana-title-revealed-leaked-pics-avoid-makers-tightens-surveillance-on-set-101715910807771.html |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240526194229/https://www.hindustantimes.com/entertainment/bollywood/ranbir-kapoor-ramayana-title-revealed-leaked-pics-avoid-makers-tightens-surveillance-on-set-101715910807771.html |archive-date=26 May 2024 |access-date=16 March 2025 |work=Hindustan Times |language=en-us |url-status=live }}</ref> On 5 April, pictures from the sets, featuring pictures of actors Arun Govil, Lara Dutta and Sheeba Chaddha and director Tiwari, were leaked onto social media and went viral.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Ranbir Kapoor Fans ANGRY As Lara Dutta, Arun Govil's Photos From Ramayana Sets LEAKED |url=https://www.news18.com/movies/ranbir-kapoor-fans-angry-lara-dutta-arun-govil-photos-from-ramayana-sets-leaked-8840620.html |access-date=19 February 2025 |website=News18 |language=en |archive-date=3 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250703113725/https://www.news18.com/movies/ranbir-kapoor-fans-angry-lara-dutta-arun-govil-photos-from-ramayana-sets-leaked-8840620.html |url-status=live }}</ref><ref name="NDTVSets2024" /> Due to this, the makers imposed a strict no-phone policy on the movie sets.<ref name=":13">{{Cite web |date=5 April 2024 |title=Exclusive: 'Ramayana' director Nitesh Tiwari imposes no-phone policy on set |url=https://www.indiatoday.in/movies/bollywood/story/nitesh-tiwari-no-phone-policy-ramayana-set-ranbir-kapoor-look-ram-2523698-2024-04-05 |access-date=19 February 2025 |website=India Today |language=en |archive-date=3 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250703113725/https://www.indiatoday.in/movies/bollywood/story/nitesh-tiwari-no-phone-policy-ramayana-set-ranbir-kapoor-look-ram-2523698-2024-04-05 |url-status=live }}</ref> On 27 April, pictures of Kapoor and Pallavi were again leaked from the sets.<ref name=":14">{{Cite web |title=Crazy Viral Pics Of Ranbir Kapoor And Sai Pallavi From The Sets Of Nitesh Tiwari's Ramayana |url=https://www.ndtv.com/entertainment/crazy-viral-pics-of-ranbir-kapoor-and-sai-pallavi-from-the-sets-of-nitesh-tiwaris-ramayana-5535127 |access-date=16 March 2025 |website=www.ndtv.com |language=en |archive-date=3 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250703113725/https://www.ndtv.com/entertainment/crazy-viral-pics-of-ranbir-kapoor-and-sai-pallavi-from-the-sets-of-nitesh-tiwaris-ramayana-5535127 |url-status=live }}</ref><ref name=":15">{{Cite news |date=27 April 2024 |title='Ramayana': Ranbir Kapoor- Sai Pallavi's looks get leaked, fans gush about regal appearance |url=https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/magazines/panache/ramayana-ranbir-kapoor-sai-pallavis-looks-get-leaked-fans-gush-about-regal-appearance/articleshow/109644786.cms?from=mdr&from=mdr |access-date=16 March 2025 |work=The Economic Times |issn=0013-0389 |archive-date=6 January 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260106054420/https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/magazines/panache/ramayana-ranbir-kapoor-sai-pallavis-looks-get-leaked-fans-gush-about-regal-appearance/articleshow/109644786.cms?from=mdr&from=mdr |url-status=live }}</ref> On 30 April, the second schedule commenced in [[Mumbai]]. Yash was a part of the schedule, with Pallavi, Kapoor and Deol reportedly joining later.<ref>{{Cite news |date=30 April 2025 |title=Yash kicks off month-long shoot for Nitesh Tiwari's 'Ramayana' in Mumbai; Sai Pallavi, Ranbir Kapoor and Sunny Deol to join soon- Report |url=https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/entertainment/hindi/bollywood/news/yash-kicks-off-month-long-shoot-for-nitesh-tiwaris-ramayana-in-mumbai-sai-pallavi-ranbir-kapoor-and-sunny-deol-to-join-soon-report/articleshow/120768503.cms |access-date=11 July 2025 |work=The Times of India |issn=0971-8257 |archive-date=3 August 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260803060311/https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/entertainment/hindi/bollywood/news/yash-kicks-off-month-long-shoot-for-nitesh-tiwaris-ramayana-in-mumbai-sai-pallavi-ranbir-kapoor-and-sunny-deol-to-join-soon-report/articleshow/120768503.cms |url-status=live }}</ref> In August, [[Terry Notary]] confirmed that he was working as the action director.<ref name=":16">{{Cite web |date=23 August 2024 |title=Avatar, Avengers Endgame veteran Terry Notary working on Ranbir Kapoor's Ramayana as action director |url=https://indianexpress.com/article/entertainment/bollywood/avatar-avengers-endgame-veteran-terry-notary-working-on-ranbir-kapoors-ramayana-as-action-director-9528803/ |access-date=16 March 2025 |website=The Indian Express |language=en |archive-date=3 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250703113725/https://indianexpress.com/article/entertainment/bollywood/avatar-avengers-endgame-veteran-terry-notary-working-on-ranbir-kapoors-ramayana-as-action-director-9528803/ |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |date=23 August 2024 |title='Ramayana': Avengers Endgame stunt coordinator Terry Notary CONFIRMS working on the Ranbir Kapoor starrer - WATCH video |url=https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/entertainment/hindi/bollywood/news/ramayana-avengers-endgame-stunt-coordinator-terry-notary-confirms-working-on-the-ranbir-kapoor-starrer-watch-video/articleshow/112740067.cms |access-date=16 March 2025 |work=The Times of India |issn=0971-8257}}</ref> In May 2025, Guy Norris, known for his work on ''[[Furiosa: A Mad Max Saga]]'' and ''[[The Suicide Squad (film)|The Suicide Squad]]'', was announced as the film's stunt director for its large-scale action sequences and was closely working with Yash to accomplish the same.<ref name=":17">{{Cite web |last=Ramachandran |first=Naman |date=29 May 2025 |title=Yash Teams With 'Mad Max' Stunt Maestro Guy Norris for Epic 'Ramayana' Action Sequences (Exclusive) |url=https://variety.com/2025/film/news/yash-mad-max-guy-norris-ramayana-1236411803/ |access-date=19 June 2025 |website=Variety |language=en-US |archive-date=19 June 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250619122222/https://variety.com/2025/film/news/yash-mad-max-guy-norris-ramayana-1236411803/ |url-status=live }}</ref><ref name="Hindu_Crew">{{Cite news |date=5 July 2025 |title=All the international talent working on Ranbir Kapoor-Yash starrer 'Ramayana' |url=https://www.thehindu.com/entertainment/movies/all-the-international-talent-working-on-ranbir-kapoor-yash-starrer-ramayana/article69776300.ece |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250724163243/https://www.thehindu.com/entertainment/movies/all-the-international-talent-working-on-ranbir-kapoor-yash-starrer-ramayana/article69776300.ece |archive-date=24 July 2025 |access-date=3 August 2026 |work=[[The Hindu]]}}</ref> Principal photography for the first part [[Wrap (filmmaking)|wrapped]] by 1 July.<ref name=":18">{{Cite web |title=Ramayana: Part I - Ranbir Kapoor And Ravi Dubey Hug It Out As They Wrap Up Shoot For Nitesh Tiwari's Film |url=https://www.ndtv.com/entertainment/ramayana-part-i-ranbir-kapoor-and-ravi-dubey-hug-it-out-as-they-wrap-up-shoot-for-nitesh-tiwaris-film-8811838 |access-date=4 July 2025 |website=NDTV |language=en |archive-date=3 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250703123612/https://www.ndtv.com/entertainment/ramayana-part-i-ranbir-kapoor-and-ravi-dubey-hug-it-out-as-they-wrap-up-shoot-for-nitesh-tiwaris-film-8811838 |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |access-date=1 July 2025 |title=Ramayana: Part 1 wraps shoot; Ranbir Kapoor celebrates, cuts cake with Nitesh Tiwari |url=https://www.cinemaexpress.com/hindi/news/2025/Jul/01/ramayana-part-1-wraps-shoot-ranbir-kapoor-celebrates-cuts-cake-with-nitesh-tiwari |website=Cinema Express |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260928130018/https://www.cinemaexpress.com/hindi/news/2025/Jul/01/ramayana-part-1-wraps-shoot-ranbir-kapoor-celebrates-cuts-cake-with-nitesh-tiwari |archive-date=28 September 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref>

=== Post-production ===
The film was reportedly in post-production for 600 days.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Nitesh Tiwari's Ramayana To Take Over 600 Days In Post-production? What We Know |url=https://www.news18.com/movies/nitesh-tiwaris-ramayana-to-take-over-600-days-in-post-production-what-we-know-8892977.html |access-date=16 May 2024 |website=News18 |language=en |archive-date=16 May 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240516172032/https://www.news18.com/movies/nitesh-tiwaris-ramayana-to-take-over-600-days-in-post-production-what-we-know-8892977.html |url-status=live }}</ref> [[Visual effects]] were handled by [[DNEG]] who also co-produced the film.<ref>{{cite web |access-date=30 July 2026 |title='Ramayana' VFX, stunts, and motion capture: Meet the three Hollywood experts behind the magic |url=https://www.theweek.in/news/entertainment/2026/07/30/hollywood-experts-in-ramayana.html |website=The Week |archive-date=30 July 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260730192902/https://www.theweek.in/news/entertainment/2026/07/30/hollywood-experts-in-ramayana.html |url-status=live }}</ref>
==Music==
{{Main|Ramayana: Part 1 (soundtrack)}}
The [[film score]] and soundtrack are composed by [[Hans Zimmer]] and [[A. R. Rahman]], marking Zimmer's debut work in Indian cinema. Rahman had described the creative process as "terrifying" and "complicated" due to the epic's cultural significance, noting that the duo is working to blend Zimmer's soundscapes with traditional Indian elements.<ref name=":4" /><ref>{{Cite web |date=14 October 2025 |title=AR Rahman says Hans Zimmer asked all the 'right questions' about Ramayana: 'Who is this character?' |url=https://www.hindustantimes.com/entertainment/music/ar-rahman-says-hans-zimmer-asked-all-the-right-questions-about-ramayana-nitesh-tiwari-ranbir-kapoor-yash-sai-pallavi-101760434046713.html |access-date=31 March 2026 |website=Hindustan Times |language=en |archive-date=7 December 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251207080200/https://www.hindustantimes.com/entertainment/music/ar-rahman-says-hans-zimmer-asked-all-the-right-questions-about-ramayana-nitesh-tiwari-ranbir-kapoor-yash-sai-pallavi-101760434046713.html |url-status=live }}</ref> The score features the integration of [[Sanskrit]] verses, which Rahman added to the initial thematic soundscapes developed by Zimmer. Additionally, poet and lyricist [[Kumar Vishwas]] contributed lyrics inspired by the film's narrative.<ref name=":5" /><ref>{{cite web |access-date=9 July 2025 |title=Kumar Vishwas Pens Lyrics for A.R. Rahman and Hans Zimmer's Soundtrack in Nitesh Tiwari's Ramayana |url=https://thewire.in/ptiprnews/kumar-vishwas-pens-lyrics-for-a-r-rahman-and-hans-zimmers-soundtrack-in-nitesh-tiwaris-ramayana |website=The Wire |archive-date=15 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250715192453/https://thewire.in/ptiprnews/kumar-vishwas-pens-lyrics-for-a-r-rahman-and-hans-zimmers-soundtrack-in-nitesh-tiwaris-ramayana |url-status=live }}</ref> Karthik Netha adapted the lyrics in Tamil, Rakendu Mouli in Telugu, Vinayak Sasikumar in Malayalam and [[Karthik Saragur]] in Kannada.<ref>{{cite news |access-date=29 October 2026 |title=Ramayana unveils Judi Jodi on Karwa Chauth, celebrates Rama-Sita's sacred union |url=https://www.indiatoday.in/amp/movies/bollywood/story/ramayana-judi-jodi-song-ranbir-kapoor-sai-pallavi-karwa-chauth-3027553-2026-10-29 |work=India Today}}</ref>

In July 2026, [[T-Series (company)|T-Series]] acquired music rights to both parts of the film in a deal worth around ₹75 crore.<ref>{{cite web|title=Mega Exclusive: T-Series bags music rights to BOTH parts of Ramayana for Rs. 75 crores in an advance deal|website=[[Bollywood Hungama]]|date=28 July 2026|access-date=30 July 2026|url=https://www.bollywoodhungama.com/news/bollywood/mega-exclusive-t-series-bags-music-rights-to-both-parts-of-ramayana-for-rs-75-crores-in-an-advance-deal/|archive-date=29 July 2026|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260729174550/https://www.bollywoodhungama.com/news/bollywood/mega-exclusive-t-series-bags-music-rights-to-both-parts-of-ramayana-for-rs-75-crores-in-an-advance-deal/|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|title=Ranbir Kapoor's Ramayana bags Rs 75 cr T-Series music deal ahead of trailer drop: Report|website=[[The Indian Express]]|date=29 July 2026|access-date=30 July 2026|url=https://www.indianexpress.com/article/entertainment/bollywood/ramayana-t-series-music-rights-rs-75-crore-advance-trailer-release-date-10808273|archive-date=30 July 2026|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260730075700/https://indianexpress.com/article/entertainment/bollywood/ramayana-t-series-music-rights-rs-75-crore-advance-trailer-release-date-10808273/|url-status=live}}</ref> The first single titled "Jai Jai Ram" was released on 14 September 2026, coinciding with [[Ganesh Chaturthi]].<ref>{{cite web |access-date=14 September 2026 |title=Ramayana first song 'Jai Jai Ram': AR Rahman-Arijit Singh-Shreya Ghoshal celebrate Shri Ram |url=https://indianexpress.com/article/entertainment/bollywood/ramayana-first-song-jai-jai-ram-ar-rahman-arijit-singh-shreya-ghoshal-celebrate-shri-ram-10877144/ |website=[[The Indian Express]] |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261017134905/https://indianexpress.com/article/entertainment/bollywood/ramayana-first-song-jai-jai-ram-ar-rahman-arijit-singh-shreya-ghoshal-celebrate-shri-ram-10877144/ |archive-date=17 October 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> The second single titled "Ravana Tandav" was released on 20 October 2026, coinciding with [[Dussehra]].<ref>{{cite web |access-date=20 October 2026 |title=Ramayana: Yash unleashes Ravana's fury in Shiv Tandav Stotram on Dussehra. Watch |url=https://www.indiatoday.in/amp/movies/bollywood/story/ramayana-yash-ravana-rise-of-asura-shiv-tandav-dussehra-reveal-ranbir-kapoor-3021643-2026-10-20 |website=[[India Today]] |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261027063743/https://www.indiatoday.in/amp/movies/bollywood/story/ramayana-yash-ravana-rise-of-asura-shiv-tandav-dussehra-reveal-ranbir-kapoor-3021643-2026-10-20 |archive-date=27 October 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> The full album was released at the event held on 21 October 2026 in [[Chennai Trade Centre]], [[Nandambakkam]].<ref>{{cite web |access-date=21 October 2026 |title='I Had A Slip Of Tongue': Ranbir Kapoor Apologises For Dussehra Speech Gaffe At Ramayana Chennai Event |url=https://www.ndtv.com/entertainment/i-had-a-slip-of-tongue-ranbir-kapoor-apologises-for-dussehra-speech-gaffe-at-ramayana-chennai-event-12216904 |work=NDTV |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261025180810/https://www.ndtv.com/entertainment/i-had-a-slip-of-tongue-ranbir-kapoor-apologises-for-dussehra-speech-gaffe-at-ramayana-chennai-event-12216904 |archive-date=25 October 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |access-date=22 October 2026 |title=AR Rahman leads musical showcase of Ramayana in Chennai |url=https://www.dtnext.in/amp/story/entertainment/cinema/ar-rahman-leads-musical-showcase-of-ramayana-in-chennai |work=DT Next}}</ref>

== Marketing ==
On 6 November 2024, Malhotra officially announced ''Ramayana: Part 1'' and ''Part 2'' through a poster, along with the release windows for both films.<ref name=":2" /><ref>{{Cite news |date=6 November 2024 |title=Ranbir Kapoor's Ramayana Part 1 and 2 officially announced: See first poster, check release date details |url=https://www.hindustantimes.com/entertainment/bollywood/ranbir-kapoors-ramayana-part-1-and-2-officially-announced-see-first-poster-check-release-date-details-101730869129007.html |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250312170029/https://www.hindustantimes.com/entertainment/bollywood/ranbir-kapoors-ramayana-part-1-and-2-officially-announced-see-first-poster-check-release-date-details-101730869129007.html |archive-date=12 March 2025 |access-date=16 March 2025 |work=Hindustan Times |language=en-us |url-status=live }}</ref> Malhotra had repeatedly marketed the project as a global film, presenting an Indian subject but for the world.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Ramayana's Producer Namit Malhotra Says Its 'Massive Responsibility' To Present The Film At Global Stage |url=https://www.news18.com/movies/ramayanas-producer-namit-malhotra-says-its-massive-responsibility-to-present-the-film-at-global-stage-aa-9245773.html |access-date=16 March 2025 |website=News18 |language=en |archive-date=9 April 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250409123439/https://www.news18.com/movies/ramayanas-producer-namit-malhotra-says-its-massive-responsibility-to-present-the-film-at-global-stage-aa-9245773.html |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |date=1 March 2025 |title=Ramayana producer Namit Malhotra wants Ranbir Kapoor film to be celebrated globally like Oppenheimer, Forrest Gump |url=https://www.hindustantimes.com/entertainment/bollywood/ramayana-producer-namit-malhotra-wants-ranbir-kapoor-film-to-be-celebrated-like-oppenheimer-forrest-gump-sai-pallavi-101740730843828.html#:~:text=Namit%20says%20that%20the%20effort,don't%20like%20Hollywood%20films. |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250302085950/https://www.hindustantimes.com/entertainment/bollywood/ramayana-producer-namit-malhotra-wants-ranbir-kapoor-film-to-be-celebrated-like-oppenheimer-forrest-gump-sai-pallavi-101740730843828.html#:~:text=Namit%20says%20that%20the%20effort,don't%20like%20Hollywood%20films. |archive-date=2 March 2025 |access-date=16 March 2025 |work=Hindustan Times |language=en-us |url-status=live }}</ref> The first glimpse titled "Ramayana: The Introduction" was released online on 3 July 2025 and screened in 9 Indian cities for fans. In Mumbai, Malhotra and Tiwari paid a special surprise visit to the audience and interacted with them as well.<ref>{{cite web |access-date=3 July 2025 |title=Ramayana first glimpse: Ranbir Kapoor, Yash explode on screen as Lord Ram, Ravana; 'Hollywood-level' VFX wows fans |url=https://www.hindustantimes.com/entertainment/bollywood/ramayana-first-glimpse-ranbir-kapoor-yash-explode-on-screen-as-lord-ram-ravana-hollywood-level-vfx-wows-fans-101751526412324.html |work=Hindustan Times |date=3 July 2025 |archive-date=26 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250726060525/https://www.hindustantimes.com/entertainment/bollywood/ramayana-first-glimpse-ranbir-kapoor-yash-explode-on-screen-as-lord-ram-ravana-hollywood-level-vfx-wows-fans-101751526412324.html |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=3 July 2025 |title=Nitesh Tiwari gets emotional at Ramayana first glimpse launch; Namit Malhotra promises to 'do justice to the epic' |url=https://www.hindustantimes.com/entertainment/bollywood/nitesh-tiwari-gets-emotional-at-ramayana-first-glimpse-launch-namit-malhotra-ranbir-kapoor-yash-sai-pallavi-sunny-deol-101751536289344.html |access-date=4 December 2025 |website=Hindustan Times |language=en |archive-date=3 August 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260803060444/https://www.hindustantimes.com/entertainment/bollywood/nitesh-tiwari-gets-emotional-at-ramayana-first-glimpse-launch-namit-malhotra-ranbir-kapoor-yash-sai-pallavi-sunny-deol-101751536289344.html |url-status=live }}</ref> On 26 March 2026, coinciding with [[Rama Navami|Ram Navami]], the makers announced the next phase of the film's promotional campaign, with the first glimpse of Kapoor as Rama was released on 2 April 2026,<ref>{{Cite news |date=27 March 2026 |title='Ramayana': Ranbir Kapoor's FIRST LOOK as Lord Ram to be unveiled on Hanuman Jayanti, Producer confirms |url=https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/entertainment/hindi/bollywood/news/ramayana-ranbir-kapoors-first-look-of-lord-ram-to-be-unveiled-on-hanuman-jayanti-producer-confirms/articleshow/129838699.cms? |access-date=31 March 2026 |work=The Times of India |issn=0971-8257 |archive-date=2 August 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260802092607/https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/entertainment/hindi/bollywood/news/ramayana-ranbir-kapoors-first-look-of-lord-ram-to-be-unveiled-on-hanuman-jayanti-producer-confirms/articleshow/129838699.cms |url-status=live }}</ref> coinciding with [[Hanuman Jayanti]].<ref>{{cite web |date=2 April 2026 |access-date=2 April 2026 |title='Ramayana' Rama glimpse: Ranbir Kapoor holds sway as the Lord in Nitesh Tiwari's magnum opus |url=https://www.thehindu.com/entertainment/movies/ramayana-rama-glimpse-ranbir-kapoor-holds-sway-as-the-lord-in-nitesh-tiwaris-magnum-opus/article70814123.ece |website=The Hindu}}</ref> Ahead of its public release, the makers held private preview screenings of the glimpse in the [[United States]] to promote the film internationally. The first screening took place at an IMAX theatre in [[Burbank, California|Burbank]], [[California]], on 30 March 2026, attended by Kapoor, Tiwari and Malhotra.<ref>{{Cite news |access-date=31 March 2026 |title=Ramayana: Ranbir Kapoor's 'Rama' Teaser Unveiled In LA, Videos From Event Go Viral {{!}} Watch |url=https://www.news18.com/movies/bollywood/ramayana-ranbir-kapoors-rama-teaser-unveiled-in-la-videos-from-event-go-viral-watch-ws-l-10006467.html |work=News18 |archive-date=31 March 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260331050316/https://www.news18.com/movies/bollywood/ramayana-ranbir-kapoors-rama-teaser-unveiled-in-la-videos-from-event-go-viral-watch-ws-l-10006467.html |url-status=live }}</ref> A second screening, followed by a question-and-answer session with the filmmakers, was held in [[New York City]] on 31 March 2026. During this event, Tiwari discussed the casting of Kapoor, citing the character's restrained nature, compassion, and physicality as key considerations.<ref>{{Cite news |date=1 April 2026 |title='Ramayana': Nitesh Tiwari opens up about casting Ranbir Kapoor as Lord Ram at New York City event: 'There was nobody better' |url=https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/entertainment/hindi/bollywood/news/ramayana-nitesh-tiwari-opens-up-about-casting-ranbir-kapoor-as-lord-ram-at-new-york-city-event-there-was-nobody-better/articleshow/129936280.cms |access-date=4 April 2026 |work=The Times of India |issn=0971-8257 |archive-date=3 August 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260803060245/https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/entertainment/hindi/bollywood/news/ramayana-nitesh-tiwari-opens-up-about-casting-ranbir-kapoor-as-lord-ram-at-new-york-city-event-there-was-nobody-better/articleshow/129936280.cms |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last=Bhattacharya |first=Tanisha |date=1 April 2026 |title=Amid Criticism, Ramayana Director Nitesh Tiwari Explains Why Ranbir Kapoor Is The Perfect Rama |url=https://www.ndtv.com/entertainment/amid-criticism-ramayana-director-nitesh-tiwari-explains-why-ranbir-kapoor-is-the-perfect-rama-11295231 |work=[[NDTV]] |archive-date=8 April 2026 |access-date=3 August 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260408104116/https://www.ndtv.com/entertainment/amid-criticism-ramayana-director-nitesh-tiwari-explains-why-ranbir-kapoor-is-the-perfect-rama-11295231 |url-status=live }}</ref> At the [[CinemaCon]] 2026 event in Los Angeles, Malhotra said that the film would combine elements of fantasy and human drama from films like ''[[The Lord of the Rings (film series)|The Lord of the Rings]]'' and ''[[Gladiator (2000 film)|Gladiator]]''.<ref>{{cite web |access-date=17 April 2026 |title=Film of Indian epic 'Ramayana' aims for global audience |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/india/film-indian-epic-ramayana-aims-global-audience-2026-04-17/ |publisher=[[Reuters]]}}</ref>

On 18 July 2026, an event, titled "Pratham Sankalp" was held in [[Bharat Mandapam]], [[New Delhi]] where the film's official trailer was exclusively showcased.<ref>{{cite web |access-date=18 July 2026 |title=Ramayana Delhi trailer launch: Yash delivers a RARE speech in Hindi; calls Ranbir Kapoor "phenomenal": "WHOLE of India will understand what MAGIC you have created!" |url=https://www.bollywoodhungama.com/news/features/ramayana-delhi-trailer-launch-yash-delivers-a-rare-speech-in-hindi-calls-ranbir-kapoor-phenomenal-whole-of-india-will-understand-what-magic-you-have-created/ |website=Bollywood Hungama |archive-date=19 July 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260719131357/https://www.bollywoodhungama.com/news/features/ramayana-delhi-trailer-launch-yash-delivers-a-rare-speech-in-hindi-calls-ranbir-kapoor-phenomenal-whole-of-india-will-understand-what-magic-you-have-created/ |url-status=live }}</ref> Following the event, a short clip from the trailer was leaked on various social media platforms.<ref>{{cite web |access-date=20 July 2026 |title='Ramayana' Part 1 trailer leaked after Pratham Sankalp event in Delhi, makers launch anti-piracy crackdown ahead of July 24 release – Report |url=https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/entertainment/hindi/bollywood/news/ranbir-kapoor-and-sai-pallavi-starrer-ramayana-part-1-trailer-leaked-after-pratham-sankalp-event-in-delhi-makers-launch-anti-piracy-crackdown-ahead-of-july-24-release-report/articleshow/132507072.cms |website=The Times of India |archive-date=20 July 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260720060143/https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/entertainment/hindi/bollywood/news/ranbir-kapoor-and-sai-pallavi-starrer-ramayana-part-1-trailer-leaked-after-pratham-sankalp-event-in-delhi-makers-launch-anti-piracy-crackdown-ahead-of-july-24-release-report/articleshow/132507072.cms |url-status=live }}</ref> The trailer was also showcased in the [[San Diego Comic Con]] on 23 July.<ref>{{cite web |first=Fenil |last=Seta |access-date=16 July 2026 |title=Ramayana creates HISTORY at San Diego Comic-Con: 'International superstars' Ranbir Kapoor and Yash to unveil trailer with live performances and exclusive surprises in MASSIVE 4,800-seater Ballroom 20 |url=https://www.bollywoodhungama.com/news/bollywood/ramayana-creates-history-at-san-diego-comic-con-international-superstars-ranbir-kapoor-and-yash-to-unveil-trailer-with-live-performances-and-exclusive-surprises-in-massive-4800-seater-ballroom-2/ |website=Bollywood Hungama |archive-date=16 July 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260716083058/https://www.bollywoodhungama.com/news/bollywood/ramayana-creates-history-at-san-diego-comic-con-international-superstars-ranbir-kapoor-and-yash-to-unveil-trailer-with-live-performances-and-exclusive-surprises-in-massive-4800-seater-ballroom-2/ |url-status=live }}</ref> The next day on 24 July, the trailer was set to be released worldwide on all digital platforms however it was delayed.<ref>{{cite web |access-date=11 July 2026 |title='Ramayana' trailer to premiere worldwide on July 24; makers unveil global launch date for Ranbir Kapoor, Yash and Sai Pallavi starrer |url=https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/entertainment/hindi/bollywood/news/ramayana-trailer-to-premiere-worldwide-on-july-24-makers-unveil-global-launch-date-for-ranbir-kapoor-yash-and-sai-pallavi-starrer-at-comic-con-2026/articleshow/132325404.cms |website=The Times of India |archive-date=11 July 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260711060459/https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/entertainment/hindi/bollywood/news/ramayana-trailer-to-premiere-worldwide-on-july-24-makers-unveil-global-launch-date-for-ranbir-kapoor-yash-and-sai-pallavi-starrer-at-comic-con-2026/articleshow/132325404.cms |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite web|title=Ramayana trailer postponed as Sony Pictures comes on board for global release outside India; Namit Malhotra calls it historic moment|website=[[Bollywood Hungama]]|date=24 July 2026|access-date=24 July 2026|url=https://www.bollywoodhungama.com/news/bollywood/ramayana-trailer-postponed-as-sony-pictures-comes-on-board-for-global-release-outside-india-namit-malhotra-calls-it-historic-moment/|archive-date=24 July 2026|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260724050521/https://www.bollywoodhungama.com/news/bollywood/ramayana-trailer-postponed-as-sony-pictures-comes-on-board-for-global-release-outside-india-namit-malhotra-calls-it-historic-moment/|url-status=live}}</ref> Later, the official trailer was released digitally on 30 July 2026.<ref>{{cite web |access-date=28 July 2026 |title=Namit Malhotra announces Ramayana trailer launch date and time; unveiling set for July 30 at 4:15 am IST |url=https://www.bollywoodhungama.com/news/bollywood/namit-malhotra-announces-ramayana-trailer-launch-date-and-time-unveiling-set-for-july-30-at-415-am-ist |website=Bollywood Hungama |archive-date=28 July 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260728201524/https://www.bollywoodhungama.com/news/bollywood/namit-malhotra-announces-ramayana-trailer-launch-date-and-time-unveiling-set-for-july-30-at-415-am-ist/ |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |access-date=30 July 2026 |title=Ramayana trailer: Ranbir's Ram, Yash's Raavan stand at heart of a cinematic odyssey |url=https://www.indiatoday.in/movies/bollywood/story/ramayana-trailer-ranbir-kapoor-ram-yash-raavan-stand-at-heart-of-a-cinematic-odyssey-2959376-2026-07-30 |website=India Today |archive-date=30 July 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260730004946/https://www.indiatoday.in/movies/bollywood/story/ramayana-trailer-ranbir-kapoor-ram-yash-raavan-stand-at-heart-of-a-cinematic-odyssey-2959376-2026-07-30 |url-status=live }}</ref> On 5 August 2026, an English version of the trailer with lip-synced performances using Brahma AI was released with some minor tweaks to selected shots.<ref>{{cite web |access-date= 5 August 2026 |title= Ramayana English trailer: Ranbir Kapoor voices Lord Rama in English as he takes on Ravana |url=https://indianexpress.com/article/entertainment/bollywood/ramayana-english-trailer-ranbir-kapoor-voices-lord-rama-in-english-ravana-yash-sai-pallavi-10819628/lite/ |website=Indian Express |archive-date=5 August 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260805204559/https://indianexpress.com/article/entertainment/bollywood/ramayana-english-trailer-ranbir-kapoor-voices-lord-rama-in-english-ravana-yash-sai-pallavi-10819628/lite/ |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |access-date=7 August 2026 |title=Ramayana English trailer uses Brahma AI lip-sync; fans call Ranbir Kapoor's voice the 'most accurate' |url=https://www.ibtimes.co.in/ramayana-english-trailer-uses-brahma-ai-lip-sync-fans-call-ranbir-kapoors-voice-most-accurate-904508 |website=IBTimes India}}</ref> In the same month, an exclusive 15 minutes of footage from the film was shown at the Big Cine Expo 2026 in [[Chennai]].<ref>{{cite web |first=Sakshi |last=Navare |access-date=27 August 2026 |title='Ramayana' Screens 15 Minutes of Unseen Footage for Exhibitors at Big Cine Expo 2026 |url=https://varietyindia.com/ramayana-screens-15-minutes-of-unseen-footage-for-exhibitors-at-big-cine-expo-2026/ |website=Variety India |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260920181447/https://varietyindia.com/ramayana-screens-15-minutes-of-unseen-footage-for-exhibitors-at-big-cine-expo-2026/ |archive-date=20 September 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> On 26 September 2026, a pre-release event took place in Mumbai which was attended by YouTuber [[MrBeast]] as part of a strategic global marketing campaign.<ref>{{cite web |access-date=26 September 2026 |title=Ramayana: Ranbir Kapoor Lifts Shiv Dhanush, Explains Dharma To MrBeast At Mumbai Event |url=https://www.timesnownews.com/entertainment-news/bollywood/ramayana-ranbir-kapoor-lifts-shiv-dhanush-explains-dharma-to-mrbeast-at-mumbai-event-article-156229069/amp |website=Times Now |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260927030625/https://www.timesnownews.com/entertainment-news/bollywood/ramayana-ranbir-kapoor-lifts-shiv-dhanush-explains-dharma-to-mrbeast-at-mumbai-event-article-156229069/amp |archive-date=27 September 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> On 28 September 2026, the makers released a behind-the-scenes video of Kapoor's transformation as Rama, thus coinciding with his 44th birthday.<ref>{{cite web |access-date=28 September 2026 |title=Ramayana BTS: Ranbir Kapoor transforms into Lord Rama, Sai Pallavi recalls being 'awestruck' seeing him on set |url=https://www.hindustantimes.com/entertainment/bollywood/ramayana-bts-ranbir-kapoor-transforms-into-lord-rama-sai-pallavi-recalls-being-awestruck-seeing-him-on-set-101790609873680.html |website=Hindustan Times |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260928171731/https://www.hindustantimes.com/entertainment/bollywood/ramayana-bts-ranbir-kapoor-transforms-into-lord-rama-sai-pallavi-recalls-being-awestruck-seeing-him-on-set-101790609873680.html |archive-date=28 September 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> An international trailer was released on 15 October 2026 at a special event in [[Bengaluru]].<ref>{{cite web |access-date=16 October 2026 |title=Ramayana International trailer shares a glimpse of Ranbir Kapoor as Lord Rama having an epic face off with Yash as Ravana |url=https://www.bollywoodhungama.com/amp/news/features/ramayana-international-trailer-shares-a-glimpse-of-ranbir-kapoor-as-lord-rama-having-an-epic-face-off-with-yash-as-ravana |website=Bollywood Hungama |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261016041651/https://www.bollywoodhungama.com/amp/news/features/ramayana-international-trailer-shares-a-glimpse-of-ranbir-kapoor-as-lord-rama-having-an-epic-face-off-with-yash-as-ravana/ |archive-date=16 October 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> The event was attended by the film's main cast and crew alongside Malhotra.<ref>{{cite web |access-date=16 October 2026 |title=Ranbir Kapoor Thanks Bengaluru Fans In Kannada, Praises Yash At Ramayana Event |url=https://www.ndtv.com/entertainment/ranbir-kapoor-wins-hearts-with-kannada-speech-at-ramayana-s-international-trailer-launch-12193188/amp/1 |website=NDTV |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261016063203/https://www.ndtv.com/entertainment/ranbir-kapoor-wins-hearts-with-kannada-speech-at-ramayana-s-international-trailer-launch-12193188/amp/1 |archive-date=16 October 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> On 19 October 2026, a pre-release event was held in JRC Convention Center in [[Hyderabad]].<ref>{{cite web |access-date=20 October 2026 |title='Ramayana is not just a movie...' Ranbir Kapoor, Yash and others unites in Hyderabad ahead of November 5 release |url=https://www.wionews.com/entertainment/bollywood/ramayana-is-not-just-a-movie-ranbir-kapoor-yash-and-others-unites-in-hyderabad-ahead-of-november-5-release-1792492207014/amp |website=[[WION]]}}</ref> At the event Malhotra revealed his plans of converting the duology into a franchise and further into a larger cinematic universe.<ref>{{cite web |access-date=19 October 2026 |title=Ramayana producer unveils massive universe plan with spin-offs, games, theme parks |url=https://indianexpress.com/article/entertainment/bollywood/ramayana-producer-unveils-massive-universe-plan-with-spin-offs-games-theme-parks-10928537/lite |work=The Indian Express |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261020004612/https://indianexpress.com/article/entertainment/bollywood/ramayana-producer-unveils-massive-universe-plan-with-spin-offs-games-theme-parks-10928537/lite/ |archive-date=20 October 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> On 20 October, another pre-release event was held in [[Kolkata]] where the film was declared tax-free by [[Chief Minister of West Bengal|CM]] [[Suvendu Adhikari]].<ref>{{cite web |access-date=20 October 2026 |title='Ramayana To Be Tax-Free In West Bengal,' Says Chief Minister Suvendu Adhikari |url=https://www.ndtv.com/entertainment/ramayana-to-be-tax-free-in-west-bengal-says-cm-suvendu-adhikari-12212031/amp/1 |website=NDTV |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261021065052/https://www.ndtv.com/entertainment/ramayana-to-be-tax-free-in-west-bengal-says-cm-suvendu-adhikari-12212031/amp/1 |archive-date=21 October 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> Later, Kapoor, Pallavi and Dubey also went to ''[[Kaun Banega Crorepati]]'' to promote the film alongside [[Amitabh Bachchan]].<ref>{{cite web |access-date=24 October 2026 |title=Kaun Banega Crorepati 18: Ranbir Kapoor, Sai Pallavi and Ravi Dubey to promote Ramayana on Amitabh Bachchan-hosted show |url=https://www.bollywoodhungama.com/amp/news/features/kaun-banega-crorepati-18-ranbir-kapoor-sai-pallavi-and-ravi-dubey-to-promote-ramayana-on-amitabh-bachchan-hosted-show |work=Bollywood Hungama |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261025035746/https://www.bollywoodhungama.com/amp/news/features/kaun-banega-crorepati-18-ranbir-kapoor-sai-pallavi-and-ravi-dubey-to-promote-ramayana-on-amitabh-bachchan-hosted-show/ |archive-date=25 October 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> On 1 November 2026, a special screening of the film took place in [[London]].<ref name=IT>{{cite web |access-date=2 November 2026 |title=Ramayana Part 1: After LA and London, a grand Mumbai premiere planned {{!}} Exclusive |url=https://www.indiatoday.in/amp/movies/bollywood/story/ramayana-part-1-mumbai-premiere-after-los-angeles-showcase-3030309-2026-11-02 |work=India Today}}</ref> On 3 November, special media screening took place across Mumbai.<ref>{{cite web |access-date=3 November 2026 |title=Watch: Ranbir Kapoor, Sunny Deol Make A Grand Entry At Ramayana Premiere In Mumbai |url=https://www.ndtv.com/entertainment/watch-ranbir-kapoor-sunny-deol-make-a-grand-entry-at-ramayana-premiere-in-mumbai-12278444/amp/1 |work=NDTV}}</ref> Several media and press screenings were held across Delhi and Mumbai on 4 November.<ref name=IT />

==Release==
=== Theatrical ===

''Ramayana: Part 1'' was premiered at the [[Academy Museum of Motion Pictures]] in [[Los Angeles]] on 27 October 2026.<ref>{{cite web |access-date=18 October 2026 |title=Ranbir Kapoor, Yash's Ramayana Gets Historic World Premiere At Los Angeles Academy Museum |url=https://in.mashable.com/entertainment/115134/ranbir-kapoor-yashs-ramayana-gets-historic-world-premiere-at-los-angeles-academy-museum |work=[[Mashable India]] |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261019174755/https://in.mashable.com/entertainment/115134/ranbir-kapoor-yashs-ramayana-gets-historic-world-premiere-at-los-angeles-academy-museum |archive-date=19 October 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |access-date=18 October 2026 |title=Ramayana sets October 27 LA premiere with traditional-themed red-carpet event |url=https://www.indiatoday.in/amp/movies/bollywood/story/ramayana-october-27-los-angeles-premiere-traditional-themed-red-carpet-event-ranbir-kapoor-sai-pallavi-3020181-2026-10-18 |work=[[India Today]] |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261020081725/https://www.indiatoday.in/amp/movies/bollywood/story/ramayana-october-27-los-angeles-premiere-traditional-themed-red-carpet-event-ranbir-kapoor-sai-pallavi-3020181-2026-10-18 |archive-date=20 October 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> It was theatrically released on 5 November 2026.<ref name="TH">{{cite web |access-date=12 October 2026 |title='Ramayana' Part 1 to release worldwide on November 5; advance bookings to open on Dussehra |url=https://www.thehindu.com/entertainment/movies/ramayana-part-1-to-release-worldwide-on-november-5-advance-bookings-to-open-on-dussehra/article71574072.ece/amp/ |website=[[The Hindu]] |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261012164728/https://www.thehindu.com/entertainment/movies/ramayana-part-1-to-release-worldwide-on-november-5-advance-bookings-to-open-on-dussehra/article71574072.ece/amp/ |archive-date=12 October 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |access-date=11 October 2026 |title=Ranbir Kapoor-Yash's Ramayana Part 1 to release worldwide on November 5 |url=https://indianexpress.com/article/entertainment/bollywood/ranbir-kapoor-yash-film-ramayana-part-1-to-release-worldwide-on-november-5-10916834/ |website=[[The Indian Express]] |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261015033416/https://indianexpress.com/article/entertainment/bollywood/ranbir-kapoor-yash-film-ramayana-part-1-to-release-worldwide-on-november-5-10916834/ |archive-date=15 October 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> It was initially planned to release in India two days later on 8 November, coinciding with [[Diwali]];<ref>{{Cite news |title=Ramayana to release on international screens 2 days before India, says producer Namit Malhotra |url=https://indianexpress.com/article/entertainment/bollywood/ramayana-to-release-on-international-screens-2-days-before-india-says-producer-namit-malhotra-10823301 |website=[[The Indian Express]] |date=8 August 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261027095545/https://indianexpress.com/article/entertainment/bollywood/ramayana-to-release-on-international-screens-2-days-before-india-says-producer-namit-malhotra-10823301/ |archive-date=27 October 2026 |access-date=4 November 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> however, Sony Pictures Entertainment announced the 6 November worldwide release date in early September.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Tangcay |first=Jazz |date=3 September 2026 |title='Ramayana' Sets November Release Date |url=https://variety.com/2026/film/news/ramayana-release-date-sony-1236849917/ |access-date=3 September 2026 |website=Variety |language=en-US |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261017110743/https://variety.com/2026/film/news/ramayana-release-date-sony-1236849917/ |archive-date=17 October 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> Later, the release date was preponed by a day.<ref name="TH" /> It served as the first instalment of a planned two-part epic.<ref>{{cite web |title=Mega Exclusive: Ramayana's release date REVEALED – Namit Malhotra's magnum opus to release on November 6 worldwide |url=https://www.bollywoodhungama.com/news/bollywood/mega-exclusive-ramayanas-release-date-revealed-namit-malhotras-magnum-opus-to-release-on-november-6-worldwide/ |website=[[Bollywood Hungama]] |date=5 August 2026 |access-date=5 August 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261017235504/https://www.bollywoodhungama.com/news/bollywood/mega-exclusive-ramayanas-release-date-revealed-namit-malhotras-magnum-opus-to-release-on-november-6-worldwide/ |archive-date=17 October 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> It was released in multiple languages with [[IMAX]] presentations as part of a large-scale global rollout.<ref>{{Cite web |date=27 May 2026 |title=Exclusive: Ramayana, Godzilla Minus Zero and the IMAX factor – Why October 30 is being seen as a strategic date : Bollywood News |url=https://www.bollywoodhungama.com/news/features/exclusive-ramayana-godzilla-minus-zero-and-the-imax-factor-why-october-30-is-being-seen-as-a-strategic-date/ |access-date=19 July 2026 |website=Bollywood Hungama |archive-date=23 July 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260723064002/https://www.bollywoodhungama.com/news/features/exclusive-ramayana-godzilla-minus-zero-and-the-imax-factor-why-october-30-is-being-seen-as-a-strategic-date/ |url-status=live }}</ref> The film was reportedly released across 59,000 screens worldwide, including 50,000 screens in overseas markets and 9,000 screens in India.<ref>{{cite web |access-date=7 August 2026 |title=Ramayana Targets 59,000 Screens: Biggest Worldwide Release In Indian Cinema; To Defeat Pushpa 2, RRR, Avatar 2 - Report Express |url=https://www.timesnownews.com/entertainment-news/bollywood/ramayana-targets-59000-screens-biggest-worldwide-release-in-indian-cinema-to-defeat-pushpa-2-rrr-avatar-2-report-article-155358357 |website=Times Now |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261017184259/https://www.timesnownews.com/entertainment-news/bollywood/ramayana-targets-59000-screens-biggest-worldwide-release-in-indian-cinema-to-defeat-pushpa-2-rrr-avatar-2-report-article-155358357 |archive-date=17 October 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> In [[China]], the film will reportedly release under the title ''Ramayana: The Legend of the Prince''.<ref>{{cite web |access-date=13 August 2026 |title='Ramayana': Ranbir Kapoor and Yash starrer set for November release in China; titled 'Ramayana: The Legend of the Prince' |url=https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/entertainment/hindi/bollywood/news/ramayana-ranbir-kapoor-and-yash-starrer-sets-november-release-in-china-titled-ramayana-the-legend-of-the-prince/articleshow/133199334.cms |work=The Times of India |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261026052943/https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/entertainment/hindi/bollywood/news/ramayana-ranbir-kapoor-and-yash-starrer-sets-november-release-in-china-titled-ramayana-the-legend-of-the-prince/articleshow/133199334.cms |archive-date=26 October 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> It became the first Indian film to be released in the [[ScreenX]] format.<ref>{{cite web |access-date=18 August 2026 |title=Ramayana to become first Indian film to release in ScreenX format worldwide |url=https://www.bollywoodhungama.com/news/bollywood/ramayana-to-become-first-indian-film-to-release-in-screenx-format-worldwide/ |website=Bollywood Hungama |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261024104122/https://www.bollywoodhungama.com/news/bollywood/ramayana-to-become-first-indian-film-to-release-in-screenx-format-worldwide/ |archive-date=24 October 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> In the overseas regions, the film was released under the title ''Ramayana: Rise of a Legend''.<ref>{{cite web |access-date=29 September 2026 |title='Ramayana' Part 1 officially titled 'Ramayana: Rise of a Legend'; new poster confirms November 6 international release |url=https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/entertainment/hindi/bollywood/news/ramayana-part-1-officially-titled-ramayana-rise-of-a-legend-new-poster-confirms-november-6-international-release/articleshow/134551857.cms |website=The Times of India |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261014162036/https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/entertainment/hindi/bollywood/news/ramayana-part-1-officially-titled-ramayana-rise-of-a-legend-new-poster-confirms-november-6-international-release/articleshow/134551857.cms |archive-date=14 October 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref>

===Distribution===
In July 2026, [[Dharma Productions]] acquired the film's [[North India|North Indian]] theatrical distribution rights for around {{INRConvert|250|c}}.<ref>{{cite web|title=Karan Johar's Dharma Productions locks Rs 250 cr deal to distribute Ramayana in India|website=[[The Indian Express]]|date=7 July 2026|access-date=7 July 2026|url=https://indianexpress.com/article/entertainment/bollywood/karan-johar-dharma-productions-rs-250-cr-deal-distribute-ramayana-ranbir-10775114/|archive-date=7 July 2026|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260707134006/https://indianexpress.com/article/entertainment/bollywood/karan-johar-dharma-productions-rs-250-cr-deal-distribute-ramayana-ranbir-10775114/|url-status=live}}</ref> Later, [[Sony Pictures Releasing]] acquired the overseas theatrical distribution rights.<ref>{{cite web |first=Naman |last=Ramachandran |access-date=23 July 2026 |title=Indian Epic 'Ramayana' Lands at Sony Pictures for International Distribution |url=https://variety.com/2026/film/news/ramayana-sony-pictures-international-distribution-1236819652 |website=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]] |archive-date=23 July 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260723211050/https://variety.com/2026/film/news/ramayana-sony-pictures-international-distribution-1236819652/ |url-status=live |date=23 July 2026|author-link=Naman Ramachandran}}</ref> [[Sri Venkateswara Creations]] acquired the theatrical distribution rights for [[Andhra Pradesh]] and [[Telangana]], while [[AVA Productions]] and E4 Entertainment acquired the theatrical distribution rights for [[Kerala]].<ref>{{cite web |title=Ramayana makers announce Dil Raju's SVC and AVA as South India distributors |url=https://varietyindia.com/ramayana-makers-announce-dil-rajus-svc-and-ava-as-south-india-distributors/ |website=Variety India |date=19 October 2026 |access-date=19 October 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261022150451/https://varietyindia.com/ramayana-makers-announce-dil-rajus-svc-and-ava-as-south-india-distributors/ |archive-date=22 October 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> Think Studios acquired the theatrical distribution rights for [[Tamil Nadu]], while [[Yash (actor)|Yash]]'s company, [[Monster Mind Creations]], acquired the theatrical distribution rights for [[Karnataka]].<ref>{{cite web |title=Exclusive: Ramayana's South distributors locked; Dil Raju bags Andhra-Telangana, Yash takes Karnataka, Think Studios gets Tamil Nadu, E4 Entertainment acquires Kerala |url=https://www.bollywoodhungama.com/news/bollywood/exclusive-ramayanas-south-distributors-locked-dil-raju-bags-andhra-telangana-yash-takes-karnataka-think-studios-gets-tamil-nadu-e4-entertainment-acquires-kerala/ |website=Bollywood Hungama |date=22 October 2026 |access-date=22 October 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261027054352/https://www.bollywoodhungama.com/news/bollywood/exclusive-ramayanas-south-distributors-locked-dil-raju-bags-andhra-telangana-yash-takes-karnataka-think-studios-gets-tamil-nadu-e4-entertainment-acquires-kerala/ |archive-date=27 October 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref>

=== Home media ===
Following its theatrical run, the film will begin streaming in India on [[JioHotstar]] through a pay-per-view model.<ref>{{cite web |access-date=21 October 2026 |title='Namit Malhotra's Ramayana And JioHotstar Join Hands To Reimagine Digital Access To India's Biggest Epic |url=https://www.jiostar.com/news/namit-malhotras-ramayana-and-jiohotstar-join-hands-to-reimagine-digital-access-to-indias-biggest-epic/ |work=JioStar |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261026130159/https://www.jiostar.com/news/namit-malhotras-ramayana-and-jiohotstar-join-hands-to-reimagine-digital-access-to-indias-biggest-epic/ |archive-date=26 October 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |access-date=21 October 2026 |title='Ramayana: Part One' to arrive on JioHotstar via pay-per-view after theatrical run |url=https://m.economictimes.com/industry/media/entertainment/media/ramayana-part-one-to-arrive-on-jiohotstar-via-pay-per-view-after-theatrical-run/articleshow/135095384.cms |work=The Economic Times}}</ref>

== Reception ==
=== Box office ===
''Ramayana – Part I'' grossed {{INR|642.82 crore}} worldwide. It grossed {{INR|401.42 crore}} in India and {{INR|226.33 crore}} in overseas market.<ref name="BO"/> 

On its opening day, the film earned ₹62.47 crore net at the domestic box office, and ₹121.62 crore gross worldwide.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2026-11-06 |title=Ramayana - Part I Worldwide Box Office: Ranbir Kapoor - Yash starter collects Rs. 121.62 cr globally on Day 1 : Bollywood News |url=https://www.bollywoodhungama.com/news/box-office-special-features/ramayana-part-i-worldwide-box-office-ranbir-kapoor-yash-starter-collects-rs-121-62-cr-globally-on-day-1/ |access-date=2026-11-09 |website=Bollywood Hungama}}</ref>

By the end of its opening weekend, the film had earned over ₹500 crore worldwide.<ref>{{Cite web|title=‘Ramayana: Part 1’ vs ‘Dhurandhar 2’ Box Office: Ranbir Kapoor’s epic trails Ranveer Singh’s blockbuster on opening day and lifetime run|url=https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/entertainment/hindi/bollywood/news/ramayana-part-1-vs-dhurandhar-2-box-office-ranbir-kapoors-epic-trails-ranveer-singhs-blockbuster-on-opening-day-and-lifetime-run/amp_articleshow/135679278.cms|access-date= 9 November 2026|website=[[The Times Of India]]}}</ref> The global opening weekend gross was $55.7 million, only behind ''[[Godzilla Minus Zero]]'', with $22.83 million earned from overseas markets, the highest overseas opening for any Hindi film in 2026''.''<ref>{{Cite web|title=‘Godzilla Minus Zero’ Is King Of The Global Weekend Box Office With $63M, Towers Over ‘Ramayana’s $55M+ WW Opening|url=https://deadline.com/2026/11/box-office-global-godzilla-minus-zero-ramayana-rise-of-a-legend-1237216698/|access-date= 9 November 2026|website=[[Deadline Hollywood|Deadline]]}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=2026-11-09 |title=Ramayana – Part I Box Office: Ranbir Kapoor – Yash starrer collects $22.83 million in overseas opening weekend; edges past Dhurandhar The Revenge to top 2026’s international charts |url=https://www.bollywoodhungama.com/news/box-office-special-features/ramayana-part-i-box-office-ranbir-kapoor-yash-starrer-collects-22-83-million-in-overseas-opening-weekend-edges-past-dhurandhar-the-revenge-to-top-2026s-international-ch/ |access-date=2026-11-09 |website=Bollywood Hungama |language=en}}</ref>

=== Critical response ===
While ''[[DNA India]]'' and ''[[The Economic Times]]'' characterised the reviews as positive, and ''[[The Indian Express]]'' deemed those as "largely positive", [[BBC News]] summarised that the film received mixed reviews.{{efn|Attributed to multiple references<ref>{{Cite news |date=6 November 2026 |title=''Ramayana: Part 1'' ends with Sita Haran; what to expect from Part 2 |url=https://indianexpress.com/article/entertainment/bollywood/ramayana-part-2-what-to-expect-ramayana-part-1-end-explained-10951922/ |access-date=6 November 2026 |newspaper=The Indian Express|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261107053815/https://indianexpress.com/article/entertainment/bollywood/ramayana-part-2-what-to-expect-ramayana-part-1-end-explained-10951922/ |archive-date=7 November 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |date=6 November 2026 |title=''Ramayana'' OTT release and platform details: When and where to watch Ranbir Kapoor, Sai Pallavi, Yash-starrer online after theatrical run |url=https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/magazines/panache/ramayana-ott-release-and-platform-details-when-and-where-to-watch-ranbir-kapoor-sai-pallavi-yash-starrer-online-after-theatrical-run/articleshow/135558258.cms |access-date=6 November 2026 |work=The Economic Times|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261107053927/https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/magazines/panache/ramayana-ott-release-and-platform-details-when-and-where-to-watch-ranbir-kapoor-sai-pallavi-yash-starrer-online-after-theatrical-run/articleshow/135558258.cms?from=mdr |archive-date=7 November 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Singh |first=Simran |date=6 November 2026 |title=''Ramayana'' box office collection Day 1: Despite positive reviews, Ranbir, Yash-film trails ''Adipurush'', ''Dhurandhar 2'', ''Jawan'', but beats ''Animal'', ''Pathaan'' |url=https://www.dnaindia.com/bollywood/report-ramayana-box-office-collection-day-1-despite-positive-reviews-ranbir-yash-film-trails-adipurush-dhurandhar-2-jawan-but-beats-animal-pathaan-3223671 |access-date=7 November 2026 |website=DNA India |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261107054138/https://www.dnaindia.com/bollywood/report-ramayana-box-office-collection-day-1-despite-positive-reviews-ranbir-yash-film-trails-adipurush-dhurandhar-2-jawan-but-beats-animal-pathaan-3223671 |archive-date=7 November 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last=Mateen |first=Zoya |date=5 November 2026|title=India's costliest film retells a beloved Hindu epic - but divides critics |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cm93zv62v1n7o |website=bbc.com |location=Delhi, India |publisher=BBC News |access-date=5 November 2026|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261105110701/https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cm93zv62v1n7o |archive-date=5 November 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref>}} {{Rotten Tomatoes prose|76|6.7|50|access-date={{RT data|access date}}}}<ref>{{Cite web |title=''Ramayana: Rise of a Legend'' |url=https://www.rottentomatoes.com/m/ramayana_rise_of_a_legend |access-date=7 November 2026 |website=Rotten Tomatoes |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261015225656/https://www.rottentomatoes.com/m/ramayana_rise_of_a_legend |archive-date=15 October 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> [[Metacritic]], which uses a [[Weighted arithmetic mean|weighted average]], assigned the film a score of 58 out of 100, based on nine critics, indicating "mixed or average" reviews.<ref>{{cite web |title=''Ramayana: Rise of a Legend'' |url=https://www.metacritic.com/movie/ramayana-rise-of-a-legend/ |website=Metacritic |access-date=7 November 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261105042532/https://www.metacritic.com/movie/ramayana-rise-of-a-legend/ |archive-date=5 November 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref>

Critics noticed influences in the film from the narrative of [[Marvel films]] and [[William Shakespeare]] works; the visuals of ''[[Princess Mononoke]]'' and [[Terry Gilliam]] works; the narrative and the visuals of ''[[The Lion King]]'' and ''[[The Lord of the Rings (film series)|The Lord of the Rings]]''; the aesthetics of [[Amar Chitra Katha]] and [[Raja Ravi Varma]]; the creatures of ''[[Jack the Giant Slayer]]'', ''[[X-Men (film series)|X-Men]]'' and ''[[Mad Max: Fury Road]]''; the action of ''[[Crouching Tiger, Hidden Dragon]]''; ''[[Game of Thrones]]'', ''[[KGF (film series)|KGF]]'' and [[Ramanand Sagar]]'s ''[[Ramayan (1987 TV series)|Ramayana]]''.{{efn|Attributed to multiple references<ref name="ramayana4" /><ref name="ramayana8" /><ref name="ramayana9" /><ref name="ramayana11" />}} Reviewers identified the film variously as an [[Action adventure film|action-adventure]], a [[mythological film]], a [[revenge tragedy]], or an [[Epic film|epic]] [[Melodrama (film genre)|melodrama]].<ref name="ramayana3">{{Cite news |title=''Ramayana: Part 1'' movie review: Ranbir Kapoor and Yash excel as Ravana outshines Rama on screen |url=https://www.thehindu.com/entertainment/movies/ramayana-part-1-movie-review-ranbir-kapoor-and-yash-excel-as-ravana-outshines-rama-on-screen/article71669057.ece|last=Kumar|first=Anuj|date=5 November 2026|access-date=8 November 2026|work=[[The Hindu]]|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261108091241/https://www.thehindu.com/entertainment/movies/ramayana-part-1-movie-review-ranbir-kapoor-and-yash-excel-as-ravana-outshines-rama-on-screen/article71669057.ece/amp/|archive-date=8 November 2026|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="ramayana5">{{Cite news |title=''Ramayana'' review: Can this $500m film saga live up to expectations? |url=https://www.thenationalnews.com/arts-culture/film-tv/2026/11/05/ramayana-review-500-million-film-budget-price-cast/|last=Ojha|first=Ankit|access-date=8 November 2026|work=[[The National (Abu Dhabi)|The National]]|date=5 November 2026|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261107091037/https://www.thenationalnews.com/arts-culture/film-tv/2026/11/05/ramayana-review-500-million-film-budget-price-cast/|archive-date=7 November 2026|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="ramayana8">{{Cite news |title=''Ramayana: Rise of a Legend'' review: India’s most expensive film ever becomes spectacular, huge-scale epic |url=https://www.theguardian.com/film/2026/nov/04/ramayana-rise-of-a-legend-review-indias-most-expensive-film-ever-becomes-spectacular-huge-scale-epic|last=Bradshaw|first=Peter|date=4 November 2026|access-date=8 November 2026|work=[[The Guardian]]|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261108090507/https://www.theguardian.com/film/2026/nov/04/ramayana-rise-of-a-legend-review-indias-most-expensive-film-ever-becomes-spectacular-huge-scale-epic|archive-date=8 November 2026|url-status=live|author-link=Peter Bradshaw}}</ref>

For Devesh Sharma, Tiwari knew "when to let the spectacle take over and when to step back and allow the emotions to do the talking".<ref name="ramayana13">{{Cite magazine |title=''Ramayana'' Movie Review: A Spectacle With Soul |url=https://www.filmfare.com/reviews/bollywood-movies/ramayana-movie-review-a-spectacle-with-soul-86987.amp|last=Sharma|first=Devesh|date=5 November 2026|access-date=8 November 2026|work=[[Filmfare]]|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261108090137/https://www.filmfare.com/reviews/bollywood-movies/ramayana-movie-review-a-spectacle-with-soul-86987.amp|archive-date=8 November 2026|url-status=live}}</ref> Though, while conceding that the celestial sequences looked "truly sublime", [[Sukanya Verma]] found the "scenery and sentiment" of his vision as "strictly synthetic."<ref name="ramayana9">{{Cite news |title=''Ramayana: Part 1'' Review: All Scale No Soul |url=https://m.rediff.com/movies/review/ramayana-part-1-review-all-scale-no-soul/20261105.htm|date=5 November 2026|access-date=8 November 2026|website=[[Rediff]]|last=Verma|first=Sukanya|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261108090350/https://m.rediff.com/movies/review/ramayana-part-1-review-all-scale-no-soul/20261105.htm|archive-date=8 November 2026|url-status=live}}</ref> For Ankit Ojha, the film held "something refreshing about the sincerity of its storytelling."<ref name="ramayana5" /> Though for Aishani Biswas, the screenplay struggled to give its characters and parallel threads enough emotional depth, which made the storytelling feel "uneven despite the grandeur on screen."<ref name="ramayana2">{{Cite news |title=''Ramayana'' Review: Nitesh Tiwari’s VFX Spectacle Misses The Soul |url=https://www.outlookindia.com/art-entertainment/movie-review/ramayana-rise-of-a-legend-review-nitesh-tiwaris-spectacle-of-gods-and-demons-loses-the-soul-of-the-epic|last=Biswas|first=Aishani|date=5 November 2026|access-date=8 November 2026|work=[[Outlook (Indian magazine)|Outlook]]|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261108091401/https://www.outlookindia.com/art-entertainment/movie-review/ramayana-rise-of-a-legend-review-nitesh-tiwaris-spectacle-of-gods-and-demons-loses-the-soul-of-the-epic|archive-date=8 November 2026|url-status=live}}</ref> Despite the film's penchant for having "grandiloquence and ardour" in its dialogues, Verma regarded certain lines as carrying a rather "pedestrian quality to its conceit."<ref name="ramayana9" /> Similarly, Ojha felt that the dialogues were "clunky at first, with grating exposition where a silent exchange of looks" could have conveyed more.<ref name="ramayana5" /> Anuj Kumar characterised the narrative structure as providing Rama little space to "express grief, betrayal, or confusion," making his acceptance of exile feel "mechanical, and the constant urge to know what the future holds for him" becoming another box ticked.<ref name="ramayana3" /> Biswas felt that the film was "so occupied with demonstrating the magnitude of its universe" that it occasionally forgot to give its characters "enough room to breathe", pointing out in particular Bharata and Shatrughna's limited presence.<ref name="ramayana2" /> Verma characterised Kumbhakarna as lacking "personality and voice", and most of his ilk as "one-note growlers solely existing to be bumped off by Ram and Lakshman's arsenal or arrows."<ref name="ramayana9" /> Though A. Kumar, on the other hand, thought that Ravana had a "deeply textured character arc."<ref name="ramayana3" />

Vineeta Kumar believed that Ranbir Kapoor didn't "overplay the emotional scenes," nor did he "lose his energy" when the action demanded it.<ref name="ramayana6">{{Cite news |title=''Ramayana'' review: Ranbir's Rama, Yash's Ravana in a spellbinding epic for the ages |url=https://www.indiatoday.in/amp/movies/reviews/story/ramayana-part-1-review-ranbirs-rama-yashs-ravana-in-a-spellbinding-epic-for-the-ages-3032286-2026-11-05|last=Kumar|first=Vineeta|date=5 November 2026|access-date=8 November 2026|work=[[India Today]]|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261108091049/https://www.indiatoday.in/amp/movies/reviews/story/ramayana-part-1-review-ranbirs-rama-yashs-ravana-in-a-spellbinding-epic-for-the-ages-3032286-2026-11-05|archive-date=8 November 2026|url-status=live}}</ref> Even though Rishabh Suri found similar praise for him in moving effortlessly through the action sequences, he didn't quite evoke the "sense of devotion" that Govil did in [[Ramayan (1987 TV series)|the TV series]] for him.<ref name="ramayana7">{{Cite news |title=''Ramayana Part 1'' review: Yash, Ranbir Kapoor, Sai Pallavi's spectacular film breathes new life into an epic we know by heart |url=https://www.hindustantimes.com/entertainment/bollywood/ramayana-part-1-review-yash-ranbir-kapoor-sai-pallavis-spectacular-film-breathes-new-life-into-an-epic-we-know-by-heart-101793853147143.html|last=Suri|first=Rishabh|date=5 November 2026|access-date=8 November 2026|work=[[Hindustan Times]]|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261108090852/https://www.hindustantimes.com/entertainment/bollywood/ramayana-part-1-review-yash-ranbir-kapoor-sai-pallavis-spectacular-film-breathes-new-life-into-an-epic-we-know-by-heart-101793853147143.html|archive-date=8 November 2026|url-status=live}}</ref> His dialogue delivery did not consistently convey the "authority and calm" one expects from Rama for Biswas.<ref name="ramayana2" /> Verma even declared his portrayal as bland, robotic and soulless, "restrained to the point of tense".<ref name="ramayana9" /> Meanwhile, [[Shubhra Gupta]] considered his portrayal as Parashurama to be "more impactful."<ref name="ramayana4">{{Cite news |title=''Ramayana: Part 1'' Movie Review: Ranbir Kapoor, Yash conjure up the perfect epic for this Kalyuga |url=https://indianexpress.com/article/entertainment/movie-review/ramayana-part-1-movie-review-ranbir-kapoor-namit-malhotra-perfect-epic-for-kalyuga-10951499/lite/|last=Gupta|first=Shubhra|date=6 November 2026|access-date=8 November 2026|work=[[The Indian Express]]|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261108091136/https://indianexpress.com/article/entertainment/movie-review/ramayana-part-1-movie-review-ranbir-kapoor-namit-malhotra-perfect-epic-for-kalyuga-10951499/lite/|archive-date=8 November 2026|url-status=live}}</ref> While V. Kumar praised Pallavi for carrying the action sequences with conviction, [[Taran Adarsh]] commended her for bringing "dignity and strength" to her "naturalistic performance" that provided "tenderness and warmth to the emotional moments."<ref name="ramayana6" /><ref name="ramayana12">{{Cite web |title=''Ramayana: Part I'' Movie Review: ''Ramayana'' is not merely a film, It's an Experience |url=https://www.bollywoodhungama.com/movie/ramayana-part-i/critic-review/ramayana-part-i-movie-review/ramayana-is-not-merely-a-film-its-an-experience/|date=31 October 2026|access-date=8 November 2026|website=[[Bollywood Hungama]]|last=Adarsh|first=Taran|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261108090239/https://www.bollywoodhungama.com/movie/ramayana-part-i/critic-review/ramayana-part-i-movie-review/ramayana-is-not-merely-a-film-its-an-experience/|archive-date=8 November 2026|url-status=live}}</ref> Though Verma pointed out her impassive response regarding her abduction and the fate of Jatayu.<ref name="ramayana9" /> For V. Kumar, Kapoor and Pallavi's chemistry developed organically, particularly during their journey through the forest.<ref name="ramayana6" /> Though A. Kumar lamented the fact of taking desire "out of the equation," and therefore stripping the Rama-Sita love story of "raw human impulses" and filtering it through "a clinical lens of absolute duty."<ref name="ramayana3" /> Similarly, Biswas characterised the songs as often taking the place of conversations "that could have revealed more about their connection", making their chemistry lack the emotional depth the film needed.<ref name="ramayana2" />

Despite his "repetitive, bushy beard villain brief," Yash's performance didn't slip into monotony for Verma.<ref name="ramayana9" /> Similarly, Ravana was meant to command "fear, fascination and awe in equal measure", and for V. Kumar, Yash understood that balance "rather well."<ref name="ramayana6" /> Though A. Kumar lamented the fact that the shades associated with the great scholar "are reduced to one scene." Additionally, he was found to have "beautifully dubbed" (by Kelkar) by him.<ref name="ramayana3" /> For V. Kumar, Dubey's eyes coveyed "a thousand emotions," and the clarity with which he delivered his dialogues was sharp.<ref name="ramayana6" /> For Biswas, he brought an entertaining energy, and added "warmth and a lighter touch" to the film.<ref name="ramayana2" /> Though for A. Kumar, he played his role with a "self-conscious awareness" that he was merely a "second fiddle."<ref name="ramayana3" /> Govil was found to be "pitch perfect" by Suri. Dutta was "bang on", and Chaddha cast a "lasting impression" on him, and Adarsh found Singh first-rate.<ref name="ramayana7" /><ref name="ramayana12" /> Verma, however, found all three to do "precious little" with their roles.<ref name="ramayana9" /> Krishnan was found to have "a few standout moments" by Ojha.<ref name="ramayana5" /> Agarwal was criticised by Verma.<ref name="ramayana9" /> Jatayu was found to have "powerfully voiced" (by Kher) by A. Kumar.<ref name="ramayana3" /> Kunal Kapoor made for a "rather dishy" Indra, per Sharma.<ref name="ramayana13" /> Oberoi niftily conveyed the "haughtiness of his character", for Verma.<ref name="ramayana9" /> Though for A. Kumar, he took it to the "melodrama of yore."<ref name="ramayana3" /> Shobana left a mark to Gupta.<ref name="ramayana4" /> Deo was solid, per Adarsh.<ref name="ramayana12" />

For V. Kumar, the score gave the film an "almost spiritual dimension," particularly during the action sequences and larger than life moments, making several scenes "feel considerably bigger than what is unfolding on screen."<ref name="ramayana6" /> In contrast, [[Saibal Chatterjee]] felt it could have done more by imparting "greater depth and range" to the key characters.<ref name="ramayana10">{{Cite news |title=''Ramayana'' Review: Spectacle Overshadows Substance In Ranbir Kapoor And Yash Film |url=https://www.ndtv.com/entertainment/ramayana-review-spectacle-overshadows-substance-in-ranbir-kapoor-and-yash-film-3-stars-12285603|date=5 November 2026|access-date=8 November 2026|website=[[NDTV]]|last=Chatterjee|first=Saibal|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261105181524/https://www.ndtv.com/entertainment/ramayana-review-spectacle-overshadows-substance-in-ranbir-kapoor-and-yash-film-3-stars-12285603|archive-date=5 November 2026|url-status=live}}</ref> While V. Kumar believed the songs to have found their footing once they were woven into the film's narrative, A. Kumar found them functioning as a "polished technical exercise rather than an emotional anchor."<ref name="ramayana6" /><ref name="ramayana3" /> Similarly, Verma felt that they were merely "rehashed riffs" of Rahman's previous tunes.<ref name="ramayana9" /> Additionally, "Mangal Rang" was the "most memorable track" for Renuka Vyavahare.<ref name="ramayana11">{{Cite news |title=''Ramayana: Rise of a Legend'' |url=https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/entertainment/hindi/movie-reviews/ramayana-rise-of-a-legend/movie-review/135561385.cms|last=Vyavahare|first=Renuka|date=5 November 2026|access-date=8 November 2026|work=[[The Times of India]]|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261105181616/https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/entertainment/hindi/movie-reviews/ramayana-rise-of-a-legend/movie-review/135561385.cms|archive-date=5 November 2026|url-status=live}}</ref> To Simon Abrams, the action sequences seemed either "poorly showcased or negligibly choreographed."<ref name="ramayana1">{{Cite web |title=''Ramayana: Rise of a Legend'' |url=https://www.rogerebert.com/reviews/ramayana-rise-of-a-legend-india-movie-review-2026|date=7 November 2026|access-date=8 November 2026|website=[[RogerEbert.com]]|last=Abrams|first=Simon|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261108090053/https://www.rogerebert.com/reviews/ramayana-rise-of-a-legend-india-movie-review-2026|archive-date=8 November 2026|url-status=live}}</ref> Ojha, on the other hand, considered the film to contain some of the best action choreography seen in Indian cinema.<ref name="ramayana5" /> Similarly, for Adarsh, production design created a world that stood "shoulder to shoulder with the best of global cinema."<ref name="ramayana12" /> Though A. Kumar believed that the historically and culturally nuanced landscape of Ayodhya and Lanka "demanded more layering" than the film eventually offered.<ref name="ramayana3" />

Though Suri proclaimed that the visual effects of the film can "truly stand up to any Hollywood film", V. Kumar found its use of AI-generated imagery "too obvious" and distracting occasionally, particularly the "caricature-like" rendering of Khar, Dushan and Kumbhakarna.<ref name="ramayana7" /><ref name="ramayana6" /> To Abrams though, the special effects sequences were "lifeless and neither productive nor compellingly surreal."<ref name="ramayana1" /> The runtime was "completely justified" owing to the "brisk pace" of the film, for Sharma.<ref name="ramayana13" /> While the film held Ojha's attention for the bulk of its length, Chatterjee was wore down when a surfeit of "surface gloss" led to monotony and overwhelmed the story.<ref name="ramayana5" /><ref name="ramayana10" /> The cinematography was deemed glossy by Chatterjee.<ref name="ramayana10" /> The editing was choppy for Abrams, not only during special effects sequences, but also when characters were talking to each other.<ref name="ramayana1" /> The costumes felt like a "Ramayana-inspired wedding collection" to A. Kumar. He also found the tone insufferable because of the film's decision to shift to domestic drama after "exhaustively mapping out Lanka," making the film’s emotional core feel "rushed, safe and light."<ref name="ramayana3" />

While Kapoor's portrayal was contrasted with his performance in ''[[Animal (2023 Indian film)|Animal]]'', and the visual effects were compared to that of ''[[Avatar (2009 film)|Avatar]]'', the film itself drew comparisons with ''[[Adipurush]]'', ''[[The Odyssey (2026 film)|The Odyssey]]'', two episodes of [[Shyam Benegal]]'s ''[[Bharat Ek Khoj]]'' based on [[Bhasa]]'s interpretation of the ''Ramayana'', and to the 1950s and 60s American films.{{efn|Attributed to multiple references<ref name="ramayana11" /><ref name="ramayana13" /><ref name="ramayana10" /><ref name="ramayana8" /><ref name="ramayana9" />}}

== Sequel ==
A sequel, ''Ramayana: Part 2'', is scheduled for release during Diwali 2028, having initially been announced for Diwali 2027.<ref>{{cite news |date=6 November 2026 |title=Namit Malhotra is open to making ‘Ramayana trilogy depending on audience response to part 1; confirms part 2 will release during Diwali 2028, says, 'We want to deliver the finale in the grandest way' |url=https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/articleshow/135571676.cms |access-date=8 November 2026 |work=The Times of India}}</ref> Principal photography for the second part began in March 2026 in Mumbai.<ref>{{cite web |access-date=12 March 2026 |title=Ramayana 2: Ranbir Kapoor begins shoot in Mumbai, Sunny Deol to join soon |url=https://www.indiatoday.in/movies/bollywood/story/ramayana-2-ranbir-kapoor-begins-shoot-in-mumbai-sunny-deol-to-join-soon-2880646-2026-03-12 |website=India Today |archive-date=19 April 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260419024212/https://www.indiatoday.in/movies/bollywood/story/ramayana-2-ranbir-kapoor-begins-shoot-in-mumbai-sunny-deol-to-join-soon-2880646-2026-03-12 |url-status=live }}</ref> In November 2026, [[Namit Malhotra]] confirmed the postponement, explaining that the filmmakers required additional time to complete the film given its scale.<ref>{{cite news |date=4 November 2026 |title=Ramayana producer Namit Malhotra hints at trilogy, confirms Part 2 shifted to 2028 |url=https://indianexpress.com/article/entertainment/bollywood/ramayana-producer-namit-malhotra-hints-at-trilogy-confirms-part-2-shifted-to-2028-10950159/ |access-date=8 November 2026 |work=The Indian Express}}</ref> The new release window was also announced in the end credits of ''Part 1''.<ref>{{cite news |date=5 November 2026 |title=Ramayana ends with a BIG SURPRISE: Makers CONFIRM Diwali 2028 release for Part 2 |url=https://www.bollywoodhungama.com/news/bollywood/ramayana-ends-with-a-big-surprise-makers-confirm-diwali-2028-release-for-part-2/ |access-date=8 November 2026 |work=Bollywood Hungama}}</ref>

